# ---- Worlds ----------------------------------------------------

world.carnival.desc = Sideshow booths to test your nerve with noise and nonsense.
world.carnival.name = Carnival Row
world.classic.desc = Arcade legends from the late 20th century. Screens intensionally left blank.
world.classic.name = Classic Corner
world.lab.desc = Games all around sound itself.
world.lab.name = Sound Lab
world.math.desc = Numbers, numbers, numbers! Get your numbers here, they're loverly!
world.math.name = Number Hall
world.neon.desc = Be quick! Be precise! Listen closely!
world.neon.name = Neon Alley
world.night.desc = Odd jobs. Some of them very odd indeed.
world.night.name = The Night Shift
world.open_stars = {open} of {total} open, {stars} stars: {bonus} percent more coins here.
world.puzzle.desc = You don't have to think fast to think hard.
world.puzzle.name = Puzzle Parlour
world.rhythm.desc = Musical games.
world.rhythm.name = Rhythm Row
world.space.desc = Seek out new games and new tables.
world.space.name = Deep Space
world.sports.desc = Sports, without the playing sports.
world.sports.name = Sports Arena


# ---- Games -----------------------------------------------------

game.aceyducey.desc = Two cards up: bet whether the third falls between them.
game.aceyducey.help = The dealer turns up two cards, read out, each with a tone for its rank, from a low two to a high ace. Bet whether the third card falls strictly between them: {up} and {down} raise and lower your bet by five, {right} bets all you have, and {action} places it. A bet of nothing passes the hand. Win and you get your bet back and as much again; lose and it is gone. You start with a hundred dollars, and there are twenty hands. The wider the gap, the better your chances: bet big on the wide ones and pass the narrow ones. What you finish with is your score.
game.aceyducey.name = Acey Ducey
game.aceyducey.unit = points
game.archery.desc = Draw, hold your aim against the wind, and loose for gold.
game.archery.help = Four ends of three arrows. The target hums from where it is. Aim with {left} and {right}: a click comes from where you aim, a bright ping when you are lined up. Before each end the wind is called: a breeze from the left pushes your arrow right, so aim a little into it. Hold {action} to draw the bow on a rising tone, and let go when it reaches the steady middle note, a soft pulse that tells you the draw is right: too little and the arrow drops, too much and it flies high. Gold scores ten, the rings outside it nine down to one.
game.archery.name = Archery
game.archery.unit = points
game.artillery.desc = Range the target by ear and fire.
game.artillery.help = A target sits somewhere out in front of you. Set your range with {up} and {down}: a rising tone means further, falling means nearer. Fire with {action}. The shell tells you whether it fell short or long, and you correct from there.
game.artillery.name = Artillery
game.artillery.unit = hits
game.asteroids.desc = Fly, turn and shoot in a field of rocks. After Oriol Gomez's Asteroids.
game.asteroids.help = You fly a ship in a field of space that wraps round at its edges. Turn with {left} and {right}, thrust with {up} and brake with {down}; the ship drifts as ships do. Every rock pulses from where it is compared with your nose, faster the closer it is, low for a large rock and high for a small one. When a rock is in your line of fire a lock tone sounds: fire with {action}, up to four shots at a time. Large rocks split into medium ones, medium into small. Saucers pulse as they hunt you and fire back; the small ones, later on, are quicker and deadlier. In a tight spot, {confirm} jumps into hyperspace, to somewhere at random, but one jump in six destroys the ship. Clear every rock for the next wave. Three ships, and another every ten thousand points. Hardcore has faster rocks and small saucers from the start. After Asteroids by Oriol Gomez.
game.asteroids.name = Asteroids
game.asteroids.unit = points
game.atc.desc = Land them all. Do not let two meet.
game.atc.help = You are air traffic control. Aircraft circle around you at different bearings and distances, each with its own engine note. Press its number to select it, then left or right to turn it, or down to bring it in to land. Two aircraft too close together is a disaster.
game.atc.name = Plane Control
game.atc.unit = landings
game.attack.desc = Did that note begin sharply or gently?
game.attack.help = A note plays. Press {left} if it started sharply, like a plucked string, and {right} if it swelled in gently, like a bowed one. The difference narrows as you improve. Press zero to hear it again.
game.attack.name = Hard Or Soft
game.attack.unit = correct
game.awari.desc = The ancient sowing game: six pits each, stones, and captures.
game.awari.help = Awari, an ancient African game of the mancala family. You have six pits in front of you, the computer six opposite, and each side has a store. Every pit starts with three stones. Choose a pit with {left} and {right}, its number and stones are read out, and press {action} to pick up its stones and sow them, one into each pit going round to the right, through your store. If your last stone lands in your store you move again. If it lands in an empty pit of yours, you capture it with the stones in the pit opposite. The game ends when one side's pits are empty, and the side with more in its store wins. {up} reads the computer's pits, {down} the stores. Three games.
game.awari.name = Awari
game.awari.unit = points
game.axe.desc = Spin, spin, and let it fly.
game.axe.help = Each throw has a target somewhere between five and fifteen metres away: its distance is read out and heard as a tone, higher for further. Build power by spinning: press the arrows round clockwise, up, right, down, left, and on round again. The faster you spin, the more power, heard as a rising whoosh, and power fades as soon as you slow. Press {action} to throw: the axe flies as far as your power. Land it on the target for fifty, close for twenty-five or ten. In Hardcore the distance is not read out, and power fades faster.
game.axe.name = Axe Throw
game.axe.unit = points
game.backwards.desc = Was that played in reverse?
game.backwards.help = A sound plays, either as it was made or reversed. Press {left} if it ran forwards and {right} if it ran backwards. Listen to how it begins and ends: real sounds strike and fade, reversed ones swell and stop dead. Press zero to hear it again.
game.backwards.name = Forwards Or Back
game.backwards.unit = correct
game.balloons.desc = Pop them before they drift out of reach.
game.balloons.help = Balloons squeak as they drift across the stall. Track one with {left} and {right} until it sits dead centre, then pop it with {action}. They drift faster as you go, and one that reaches the edge is gone.
game.balloons.name = Balloon Pop
game.balloons.unit = balloons
game.battleship.desc = Find their ships in the dark water before they find yours.
game.battleship.help = Two fleets hide in two seas, six squares by six, eight by eight in Hardcore: yours, placed for you, and the computer's. Take turns firing. Move your sights with {dirs}: columns run from your left to your right and every row has its own pitch, higher towards the top. Press {action} to fire. A hit explodes, a miss splashes, and a sunk ship is announced; one of yours going down groans and sinks into the water. A square you have already tried gives a dull knock. Press {status} to hear where you are aiming. Then the computer fires back into your sea. Sink its whole fleet to win the battle; lose yours and the game is over.
game.battleship.name = Battleship
game.battleship.unit = points
game.bearings.desc = Point straight at the sound.
game.bearings.help = A sound calls from somewhere around you. Turn with {left} and {right} until it is directly in front, then press {action}. A low double thud means it is behind you. Pure practice at placing a sound, which every other cabinet here relies on.
game.bearings.name = Bearings
game.bearings.unit = found
game.beat.desc = Hit the beat in the right ear.
game.beat.help = Notes fly at you from the left, centre and right. Press A or {left} for left, {action} for centre, L or {right} for right, exactly when the note lands: a short click from its side warns you one beat early, so wait one beat and press. Three misses and you are out. In Hardcore the notes come closer together.
game.beat.name = Beat Blaster
game.beat.unit = points
game.beatstar.desc = Hear the phrase over the band, then play it back in time.
game.beatstar.help = A band plays, and each round a phrase of notes is played over it. Then a rising go cue sounds, and you play the phrase back on the arrows, in time with the band. Each arrow is a note of the chord: {up} the low root, in the middle; {right} the third, on your right; {down} the fifth, in the middle; {left} the high octave, on your left. A note counts if you press its arrow close to its moment in the phrase: the shorter the note, the tighter the timing, and the closer you are the more it scores. Clear enough rounds without a miss and the level is cleared: the band changes style, the tempo rises, the key and the beats to the bar may change, and quicker notes creep in. A round with a miss costs part of a life, up to one, and is played again; a clean level with good timing earns a life. A long run of perfect notes brings Star Power, double points for two rounds. Press {confirm} to hear your level, lives and score. After Dynamic Beatstar by Oriol Gomez.
game.beatstar.name = Beatstar
game.beatstar.unit = points
game.beeps.desc = A quick burst of beeps. How many?
game.beeps.help = A quick burst of beeps plays: count them, type how many and press {confirm}. Backspace corrects, {up} and {down} change the number one at a time, and {action} plays the burst again, costing time. The bursts get longer and quicker as you go. A wrong count or running out of time costs one of three lives. In Hardcore the beeps change pitch and come even faster.
game.beeps.name = Beep Counter
game.beeps.unit = correct
game.berzerk.desc = Shoot your way out of the robot maze.
game.berzerk.help = A grid of rooms full of robots. Arrow keys move. Space echolocates: a click from each wall, louder the closer it is; enter tells you how far the exit is and how many robots are left. One to four fire north, east, south or west. Robots clank with every step as they hunt you. Find the exit chime and get out before they surround you.
game.berzerk.name = Berzerker
game.berzerk.unit = points
game.biggersum.desc = Two sums. Which is bigger, left or right?
game.biggersum.help = Two sums are read out, first the left one, then the right one. Press {left} or {right} for the bigger of the two, as fast as you can: the quicker, the more it scores. {action} hears them again. A wrong side, or taking too long, costs one of three lives. The sums grow as you go. In Hardcore they mix adding, taking away and times, and there is less time.
game.biggersum.name = Bigger Sum
game.biggersum.unit = correct
game.birdsong.desc = Four birds sing, one of them twice: name the one that repeated.
game.birdsong.help = Each round, birds sing one after another, each with its own little call: a rise, a fall, a trill or a chirp, at its own pitch. One bird sings twice. Press the number of the bird that sang twice, 1 for the first to sing, 2 for the second and so on. Press {action} to hear the round again. Three wrong answers end the game; the rounds grow from four birds to six, and the calls come closer together.
game.birdsong.name = Bird Song
game.birdsong.unit = points
game.blackjack.desc = Twenty-one, or as close as you dare.
game.blackjack.help = You start with a hundred chips and bet ten on every hand, twenty in Hardcore. Your cards are read out, and so is the one card the dealer shows. Get closer to twenty-one than the dealer without going over: number cards count their number, kings, queens and jacks count ten, and an ace counts eleven or one. Press {action} to take another card and {confirm} to stand. On your first move, D doubles your bet for exactly one more card. The dealer draws until reaching seventeen. A blackjack, twenty-one with your first two cards, pays three to two. Your score is your chips; you are done when you cannot cover a bet, or after five minutes. Press {status} at any time to hear how many chips you have. In Hardcore the dealer also draws on a soft seventeen and a blackjack pays six to five.
game.blackjack.name = Blackjack
game.blackjack.unit = points
game.boing.desc = Keep the ball alive, one bounce at a time.
game.boing.help = A ball bounces. Press {action} at the exact moment it touches down to send it higher. The pitch of its hum tells you how high it is; the bounce gets faster and the window gets tighter. Miss twice and it rolls away.
game.boing.name = Boing
game.boing.unit = bounces
game.bombsaway.desc = Release ahead of the target and let the bomb fall onto it.
game.bombsaway.help = You fly a bomber over targets on the ground. Each target hums as it slides beneath you from the right to the left. A bomb takes a moment to fall, so press {action} to release a little before the target is right under you, in the middle. Anti-aircraft fire crackles now and then: climb out of it with {up} as soon as you hear it, or take damage; three hits and you turn for home. Twenty-five targets; a direct hit scores most.
game.bombsaway.name = Bombs Away
game.bombsaway.unit = points
game.bounce.desc = Each bounce comes quicker. Hear two, then tap the rest in time.
game.bounce.help = A ball is dropped and bounces, each bounce a little lower and a little quicker than the last, the way a real ball does. You hear the first two bounces. Then the bounces go quiet, and you tap {action} on each of the next six, just when you think it lands: the gaps keep shrinking by the same share each time. Right on the bounce scores most. Eight balls, some bouncier than others.
game.bounce.name = Bouncing Ball
game.bounce.unit = points
game.bowling.desc = Ten frames, ten pins, and the pins sing where they stand.
game.bowling.help = Ten pins stand in a triangle at the end of the lane. Before each ball the pins still standing chime across the lane, from your left to your right. Aim with {left} and {right}: your aim ticks from where you are pointing. Press {action} to bowl. A ball knocks the pins in its path, and falling pins can take their neighbours with them. Press {confirm} to hear the pins again. Ten frames of two balls each, scored like real bowling: a strike or a spare adds the pins from the balls that follow. The ball is heard rolling down the lane, louder as it nears the pins, and each pin falls on its own. In Hardcore the ball hooks a little away from your aim, but you can steer it with {left} and {right} as it rolls; steer too far and it drops into the gutter.
game.bowling.name = Bowling
game.bowling.unit = points
game.boxes.desc = Keep your box, or take the offer?
game.boxes.help = Ten boxes hide ten prizes, from one point to a thousand. First choose your box: type its number, one then zero for box ten, or walk the boxes with {left} and {right} and press {action}. The other boxes then open one at a time, each one's prize read out. After every two, the banker makes you an offer: press {confirm} to take it, or {action} to keep going. Refuse every offer and you win whatever is in your own box.
game.boxes.name = Mystery Boxes
game.boxes.unit = points
game.boxing.desc = Slip the punch, counter hard, three rounds to win.
game.boxing.help = Three rounds of thirty seconds against a boxer who telegraphs his punches: a grunt comes from the side the punch is coming from. Slip away from it with {left} or {right}, to the other side, or cover up with {down}. Jab with {action}: a jab into his raised guard, which creaks as it comes up, does nothing, but a jab just after you slip a punch is a counter that hurts him three times as much. Knock him out to win early; otherwise the points decide it. His punches come quicker in later rounds.
game.boxing.name = Boxing
game.boxing.unit = points
game.breakout.desc = A wall of bricks, power-ups to catch. After Oriol Gomez's Breakout.
game.breakout.help = Move your paddle with {left} and {right}, and press {action} to launch the ball. The ball hums all the time, heard from where it is compared with your paddle, rising in pitch as it comes down towards you and brighter the faster it goes: when it is straight ahead of you, you are under it. While you move, the paddle hums too, with a scan tone that climbs with the number of rows of bricks still above you. Each row of the wall has its own pitch; some bricks are hard and take two hits. Sometimes a broken brick drops a power-up: it is named, and calls as it falls, louder as it nears you. Catch it with your paddle for a wider paddle, a slower ball, a sticky paddle that holds the ball until you launch it again, lasers that fire by themselves, more balls, or an extra life; most last thirteen seconds. Clear the wall for the next level, a little faster. Three lives. In Hardcore the ball is faster and power-ups are rarer. After Breakout by Oriol Gomez.
game.breakout.name = Breakout
game.breakout.unit = points
game.brightness.desc = Same note, different colour.
game.brightness.help = Two sounds play at the same pitch, but one is brighter. Press {left} if the first was brighter, {right} if the second was. The difference narrows as you improve. Press R to hear the pair again.
game.brightness.name = Bright Or Dull
game.brightness.unit = correct
game.bugline.desc = Bugs scuttle in from the edges. Swat the nearest.
game.bugline.help = Bugs crawl in from the left and right edges toward the centre where you stand. Each chitters as it moves, faster and higher as it nears you. Face the nearest with {left} or {right} and swat with {action} -- but only a bug close to you is in reach. Let one reach the centre and it bites. Three bites and you are overrun. The bugs come faster and more often as the shift wears on, later from both sides at once, and a swat at nothing throws you off balance for a moment.
game.bugline.name = Bug Line
game.bugline.unit = points
game.bullfight.desc = The bull charges from one side: step aside at the last moment.
game.bullfight.help = A bull charges at you, its hooves drumming from the side it comes from, louder and faster as it nears. Sweep your cape and step aside to the other side at the last moment: {left} or {right}, away from the bull. Too early and the bull follows you; too late, or the wrong way, and it knocks you down, three times and the bout is over. A pass close to the last moment brings a louder cheer and more points. Twenty-five passes win, and the bull grows quicker as you go. The bull is never hurt here: it is all in the passes.
game.bullfight.name = The Matador
game.bullfight.unit = points
game.bulls.desc = A secret number. How many digits are right, and in the right place?
game.bulls.help = A secret number of four different digits hides, five in Hardcore. Type a guess of the same length, every digit different, and press {confirm}. You hear how many digits are right and in the right place, each a bright chime, and how many are right but in the wrong place, each a wooden knock. Find it within ten guesses, eight in Hardcore: the fewer you need, the more it scores. Backspace corrects and {action} repeats your last clue. Three numbers not found and the game is over.
game.bulls.name = Bulls and Cows
game.bulls.unit = points
game.bumblebee.desc = Follow the buzz to the flowers.
game.bumblebee.help = You are a bee. A flower hums somewhere around you; turn with {left} and {right} and fly forward with up until you reach it. The hum rises as you close in. Each flower found spawns another, further off. As many as you can before the time runs out.
game.bumblebee.name = Bumblebee
game.bumblebee.unit = flowers
game.bumper.desc = Ram them, do not get rammed.
game.bumper.help = You drive a bumper car in a ring. Turn with {left} and {right}, hold up to accelerate. Rivals whirr around you: their engines get louder and higher as they close. Hit one from behind to score. Get hit from behind and you lose grip.
game.bumper.name = Bumper Cars
game.bumper.unit = points
game.cctv.desc = Twelve screens, one of them wrong.
game.cctv.help = Camera feeds cycle past you, each with its own steady hum. One of them has something moving on it, and it will not sound quite steady. Press {action} when that one is playing. Press on a quiet feed and you have cried wolf.
game.cctv.name = Camera Room
game.cctv.unit = spotted
game.change.desc = The right change, and quickly.
game.change.help = Customers buy something and hand you money. Give back the change using the coins on keys one to six: one, two, five, ten, twenty and fifty. Every coin has its own sound, and the running total is read as you go. {back} takes the last coin back, {action} repeats the price and what was paid, and {confirm} hands the change over. A wrong amount sends the customer away unhappy; three unhappy customers, or the end of the two-minute shift, and you are done. In Hardcore the shift lasts ninety seconds, the sums are bigger, and the running total is not read out: count the coins yourself.
game.change.name = Make Change
game.change.unit = points
game.checkers.desc = Draughts on an eight by eight board, captures and kings, against the computer.
game.checkers.help = Checkers, or draughts. Your pieces start on the dark squares of the three rows nearest you, the computer's on the far three. Pieces move one square diagonally forward; a king, crowned on the far row, moves forward or back. Jump over an enemy piece into the empty square beyond to take it, and keep jumping if you can; when a capture is possible, you must take it. {left} and {right} go through every move you can make, read out by the squares, and {action} makes it. {up} reads your pieces, {down} the computer's. Take all of its pieces, or leave it no move, to win. Three games.
game.checkers.name = Checkers
game.checkers.unit = points
game.checkpoint.desc = Walk in when the barrier falls silent.
game.checkpoint.help = Light barriers stand one after another on the way into the space station. Hold {up} to walk towards the next one. A barrier hums while it is on, louder as you get closer, and falls silent while it is off, with a click as it switches. Walk through only while it is silent: touch it while it hums and you are pushed back and lose one of three lives. Each barrier passed scores, and they switch faster the further you get. In Hardcore they stay off for less time.
game.checkpoint.name = Checkpoint
game.checkpoint.unit = points
game.chomp.desc = A cookie with a poisoned corner. Do not take the last bite.
game.chomp.help = A cookie of squares, rows by columns, and the top left square is poisoned. You and the computer take turns to chomp: choose a square with the arrow keys and press {action}, and that square goes, with every square below it and to its right. Whoever has to take the poisoned square loses. Each square's row and column are read as you move, and whether it is still there. {status} reads the cookie row by row. Five cookies, bigger each time.
game.chomp.name = Chomp
game.chomp.unit = points
game.chords.desc = Name what you just heard.
game.chords.help = A chord plays. Press one for major, two for minor, three for diminished, four for augmented, five for a seventh. Press zero to hear it again, and space to hear the notes spread out one at a time instead of together.
game.chords.name = Chord Reader
game.chords.unit = correct
game.chordswitch.desc = Say when the chord changes.
game.chordswitch.help = A chord holds, and every so often it changes to another. Press {action} the moment you hear it move. Do not press between changes. The changes get smaller and harder to spot.
game.chordswitch.name = Chord Switch
game.chordswitch.unit = changes
game.claw.desc = Everyone knows it is rigged. Try anyway.
game.claw.help = The claw glides back and forth across the cabinet, and the prize hums from where it sits compared with the claw: to your left, the prize is left of the claw; to your right, it is right of it. As the claw passes over the prize the hum slides into the middle, and a bright tick sounds when they line up. Press {action} on that tick to stop the claw, then {action} again to drop it. Even a perfect drop slips about one time in four; the claw is rigged, exactly as it is in real life.
game.claw.name = Claw Machine
game.claw.unit = prizes
game.climber.desc = Grab each hold on the beat.
game.climber.help = You climb a wall of moving holds. A hold swings across the stereo field; press {action} when it is directly in front of you, dead centre. Grab it and you rise. Miss and you slip. The holds swing faster the higher you get.
game.climber.name = Climber
game.climber.unit = metres
game.clock.desc = What time will it be? Clock sums, read out.
game.clock.help = A time is read out, and how long to add to it. Type the new time as four digits on the twenty-four hour clock, hours then minutes: nine fifteen is zero nine one five, half past two in the afternoon is one four three zero. Then press {confirm}. {action} hears it again. A wrong time or running out of time costs one of three lives. In Hardcore the times can go backwards, and add hours and minutes together.
game.clock.name = Time Keeper
game.clock.unit = correct
game.coconut.desc = Knock them down, one ball at a time.
game.coconut.help = Coconuts sit on posts across the stall. Sweep your aim with {left} and {right}: the target you are nearest hums, and it moves to the centre of your hearing as you line up. Throw with {action}. You get three balls per row.
game.coconut.name = Coconut Shy
game.coconut.unit = coconuts
game.codebreaker.desc = Find the secret row of tones from bright and soft clues.
game.codebreaker.help = A secret row of four different tones, chosen from eight, five in Hardcore. Build your guess slot by slot: {left} and {right} move between slots, {up} and {down} change the tone in the slot, and {action} plays your whole row. Press {confirm} to try it. For every tone in exactly the right place you hear a bright chime, and for every right tone in the wrong place a wooden knock. Crack the code within ten tries, eight in Hardcore. Three codes lost and the game is over.
game.codebreaker.name = Codebreaker
game.codebreaker.unit = points
game.coins.desc = Coins fall in the jar. How much is there?
game.coins.help = Coins drop into a jar one after another, and each kind has its own sound: a one is a low tick, a five a soft knock, a ten a bright clink and a twenty-five a ringing chime. Add them up as they fall, then type the total and press {confirm}. {action} drops them again, costing time. The jar gets fuller as you go. A wrong total or running out of time costs one of three lives. In Hardcore there are fifties too, a deep bell, and the coins fall faster.
game.coins.name = Coin Drop
game.coins.unit = correct
game.copycat.desc = Repeat the phrase, pitch and rhythm both.
game.copycat.help = A short phrase plays: four pads with their own pitches, in a rhythm. Copy it back on A, S, K and L, and get the timing roughly right too, not just the order. Phrases get longer and the timing gets stricter.
game.copycat.name = Copycat
game.copycat.unit = phrases
game.counterpoint.desc = Follow one line while another distracts you.
game.counterpoint.help = Two melodies play together, one in each ear. Follow only the one on your left and press {action} whenever it repeats a note. Ignore the right entirely, which is far harder than it sounds.
game.counterpoint.name = Two At Once
game.counterpoint.unit = caught
game.counting.desc = How many was that?
game.counting.help = A burst of beeps plays, sometimes slowly, sometimes far too fast to be fair. Type how many there were and press {confirm}. They get quicker and they start hiding beeps inside noise.
game.counting.name = Count The Beeps
game.counting.unit = correct
game.cubehop.desc = Hop the pattern without repeating a square.
game.cubehop.help = You hop around a small board with {dirs}. Every square you land on chimes once and turns over. Land on one twice and you lose a life. Each time you land, the four squares around you sound in turn, left, up, right and down, from their direction: a bright tick is a square still to turn, a dull thud is one already turned, and a soft brush is the edge of the board. Press {action} to hear them again and have the open directions read out. Press {confirm} to hear the whole board, row by row from the far side to yours, each square from its place: a bright tick for open, a dull thud for turned, and a high chime for where you stand. Turn over every square to clear the board. Each board has its own time, more for bigger boards, with a warning ten seconds before the end; running out costs a life and gives you a fresh board. Clear ten boards to win.
game.cubehop.name = Cube Hop
game.cubehop.unit = boards
game.cups.desc = Follow the ball under the shuffling cups.
game.cups.help = A ball is placed under one cup, and you hear where. The cups then swap, each swap sounding as a slide between two positions. Follow it, then press the number of the cup you think holds the ball. More cups and faster swaps every round.
game.cups.name = Cup Tap
game.cups.unit = rounds
game.curb.desc = Cross the traffic without looking.
game.curb.help = Five lanes of traffic run in front of you. Press up to step forward one lane, down to step back. Cars roar past in the lane you are standing in and in the one ahead: listen for a gap before you commit. Reach the far side to score.
game.curb.name = Curb
game.curb.unit = crossings
game.curling.desc = Slide the stone to the button, and sweep.
game.curling.help = The house calls from where it is, thirty metres away. Aim with {left} and {right} until the lock ping, hold {action} for the weight of your throw and let go. The stone rumbles away, lower as it slows; tap {down} quickly to sweep in front of it and carry it further. Where it stops scores: ten on the button, six, three and one for the rings, nothing outside the house. Two ends of six stones. Hardcore has a narrower house.
game.curling.name = Curling
game.curling.unit = points
game.darts.desc = Two swings to line up, one throw.
game.darts.help = Your hand sweeps side to side on its own, then up and down. Press {action} once to lock the sideways position, again to lock the height, and the dart flies. The board hums from its centre so you can hear where you are pointing.
game.darts.name = Darts
game.darts.unit = points
game.decant.desc = Sort the liquids by their pitch.
game.decant.help = Several tubes hold coloured liquid, and each colour has its own pitch. Move between tubes with {left} and {right}: each tube plays its layers one at a time, from the bottom up, so the last note you hear is the one on top. {action} plays the current tube again. Press {up} or {confirm} to pick a tube to pour from, then move to another tube and press {down} or {confirm} to pour into it, so the arrows alone are enough. You can also press a tube's number directly. A pour only works onto the same pitch or into an empty tube. Sort every tube into one pure colour.
game.decant.name = Decant
game.decant.unit = points
game.defender.desc = Catch the falling pods before they hit.
game.defender.help = Escape pods drop and you must be under them when they land. Move with {left} and {right}. A pod clicks faster the closer it is to the ground, and it is centred in your hearing when you are under it. Miss three and the colony is done for.
game.defender.name = Defender
game.defender.unit = pods
game.defuse.desc = Cut the wire that does not belong.
game.defuse.help = Several wires hum in front of you, left to right, each with its own pitch. All of them are in tune with each other except one. Press the number of the odd wire out. Press zero to hear them again. The ticking tells you how long you have.
game.defuse.name = Bomb Defuser
game.defuse.unit = points
game.depthcharge.desc = Sonar pings, a hidden submarine, and a rack of charges.
game.depthcharge.help = A submarine hides beneath your destroyer. Your sonar pings, and the echo comes back from the side the submarine lies on, higher the shallower it runs. Steer over it with {left} and {right}, nine positions across, and set your charge's depth with {up} and {down}, nine settings, each with its own tone: match it to the echo's pitch. Drop with {action}. A miss sends back a report of which way to go. Each submarine gets six charges, and there are six submarines. The fewer charges you use, the more you score.
game.depthcharge.name = Depth Charge
game.depthcharge.unit = points
game.die.desc = Which face is on top after all that rolling?
game.die.help = A die starts with one on top, two facing you and three on your right; opposite faces always add up to seven. Then it rolls: away from you, towards you, to your left or to your right. Each roll is announced and has its own sound: a rising sweep away, a falling sweep towards you, and a sweep off to the left or right. When it stops, press the number of the face now on top. The rolls grow longer as you go; three wrong answers and the game is over. In Hardcore the rolls are not announced: follow the sounds alone.
game.die.name = Rolling Die
game.die.unit = points
game.digdeep.desc = Something is buried. Listen for the hollow.
game.digdeep.help = A field of ground in front of you, and one buried prize. Move along with {left} and {right} and press {action} to tap the ground. Solid earth thuds; a hollow rings. When you are sure, press {confirm} to dig. Wrong digs cost you time.
game.digdeep.name = Dig Deep
game.digdeep.unit = finds
game.digits.desc = Type nought, one or two, thirty times. The computer tries to guess each.
game.digits.help = Type the digits nought, one or two, thirty times, as randomly as you can. Before each one, the computer makes its guess from the patterns it has seen you make, and after it you hear whether it was right: a dull thud when it guessed you, a bright ping when it did not. By pure luck it should be right ten times in thirty. Beat that and you win; people are worse at being random than they think. Three rounds of thirty, and it keeps learning.
game.digits.name = Be Random
game.digits.unit = points
game.dive.desc = Hold your breath. Take one more pearl.
game.dive.help = Dive for pearls. Hold down to swim deeper, up to rise. Pearls chime around you at different depths. Your breath drains underwater and you hear your heartbeat quicken as it runs low. Surface to breathe. Drown and you lose everything you were carrying, so know when to go up.
game.dive.name = Pearl Dive
game.dive.unit = pearls
game.docking.desc = Line up and come in slow.
game.docking.help = A docking port hums ahead. Steer with {left} and {right} to centre it, and control your closing speed with {up} and {down}. Come in centred and slow and you dock. Come in fast, or off- centre, and you bounce off the hull.
game.docking.name = Docking Bay
game.docking.unit = dockings
game.dodge.desc = Survive the falling sky.
game.dodge.help = You drift left and right with {dirs}. Meteors scream down at you: the closer they get, the higher and louder they shriek, and their position in the stereo field is where they will land. Get out of the way. Your score is seconds survived.
game.dodge.name = Meteor Dodge
game.dodge.unit = seconds
game.doors.desc = One door leads on. The rest send you back.
game.doors.help = The dungeon is a row of rooms, and each room has several doors in a line from your left to your right. Only one leads on to the next room; every other one is cursed and sends you back to the first room, costing one of three lives. The doors never change, so remember the right ones. Choose a door with its number, or move along with {left} and {right}, each door creaking from its place, and open it with {action}. Get out of the last room to escape; the next dungeon has one more room. In Hardcore the rooms have more doors.
game.doors.name = Cursed Doors
game.doors.unit = points
game.doppler.desc = Is it moving towards you, or away?
game.doppler.help = Something passes by. Press {left} if it was coming towards you and {right} if it was going away. It gets subtler each time, and later some pass at a steady distance, which you answer with {action}.
game.doppler.name = Coming Or Going
game.doppler.unit = correct
game.dots.desc = Draw lines between dots, close boxes to claim them, against the arcade or a friend.
game.dots.help = A grid of dots, three boxes by three, four by four in Hardcore. Move between the dots with {dirs}: each dot plays a note, higher towards the top and placed by its column, then a tick for every line already drawn from it, from that line's side, high for up and low for down. Press {action}, then an arrow, to draw the line from your dot that way. Close the fourth side of a box and it is yours, and you move again. Press {confirm} to hear how many sides the boxes around your dot have, and {status} for the score. Before your first line, press T to play two players on one keyboard instead of against the arcade. Win a game to go on to the next; lose two and it is over.
game.dots.name = Dots and Boxes
game.dots.unit = points
game.drumfill.desc = Hear the fill, play it back.
game.drumfill.help = A short drum fill plays: kick on A, snare on {action}, hat on L; S plays the snare too. Play it back in the same order. Only the order matters, not the timing, so take your time. The fills get longer.
game.drumfill.name = Drum Fill
game.drumfill.unit = fills
game.ducks.desc = Shoot the birds, spare the dog.
game.ducks.help = Ducks break cover and fly across the sky around you. Turn with {left} and {right}, and fire with {action}. Each duck quacks from where it really is: overhead, behind you, far off. Listen for the doppler as it passes. When a duck gets away, your dog pops up where it went and barks at you: never shoot toward a bark, it costs you points. Three shells per duck, two in Hardcore.
game.ducks.name = Duck Season
game.ducks.unit = ducks
game.duel.desc = Read the tell, beat the draw.
game.duel.help = Your opponent telegraphs each attack with a sound. A high whistle means a high strike: duck with the down arrow. A low rumble means a low sweep: jump with up. A metallic ring means a thrust: block with {action}. React before the strike lands. Five duellists stand between you and the champion, five rounds each, every one quicker than the last; beat the champion to win.
game.duel.name = Sound Duel
game.duel.unit = points
game.echoes.desc = Map a cavern with sonar alone.
game.echoes.help = You are in a pitch-black cavern. Hold up to move forward, {left} and {right} to turn, and press {action} to send a ping. The echo comes back from whatever it hit, at the angle and delay of the real thing: near walls answer fast and bright, far ones slow and dull. Find the crystals and get out.
game.echoes.name = Echoes
game.echoes.unit = points
game.echoloc.desc = Ping the dark, judge the echo, and strike the hidden target.
game.echoloc.help = Something is hidden on a grid of nine by nine. Press {action} to ping: the echo comes back from the target's side, later and fainter the further away it is, and higher if it is ahead of you, lower if it is behind. Move with {dirs}, a step a press. When you think you are on it, press {confirm} to strike: right on it scores the most, and fewer pings score more; a miss tells you how many steps away it was. Three misses and the game is over.
game.echoloc.name = Echo Location
game.echoloc.unit = points
game.egghunt.desc = Gather eggs across a field you navigate by ear.
game.egghunt.help = Walk with {dirs}. Up goes north, down goes south, left goes west, right goes east, and the field never rotates under you. Eggs chime all around the field; walk onto one to collect it. Grab two eggs quickly and the second is worth more. Five eggs in a hurry earns a speed boost. Clocks tick, and give you extra time. And listen for the chicken: if it catches you it drags you away and eats your clock. Just after you grab a clock, you can chase the chicken down and walk it over to get rid of it. Press {action} at any time to be told where the nearest egg and the chicken are. A low double thud means something is behind you, to the south.
game.egghunt.name = Egg Hunter
game.egghunt.unit = eggs
game.eights.desc = Be first to empty your hand, matching suit or number, eights wild.
game.eights.help = You and the dealer each hold seven cards, with one face up on the pile. Play a card of the same suit or the same number as the top card; an eight can be played on anything, and then you choose the suit that must follow. {left} and {right} move along your hand, and each card is named with its suit's own note: hearts highest, then diamonds, clubs, and spades lowest. Press {action} to play the card, and {confirm} to draw one when you cannot play, or to pass after drawing. After an eight, {up} and {down} choose the suit and {action} picks it. Press {status} for the top card and how many cards the dealer holds. Empty your hand first to win the hand; lose three hands and the game is over.
game.eights.name = Crazy Eights
game.eights.unit = points
game.elevator.desc = Take them where they asked to go.
game.elevator.help = Passengers get in and name a floor. Move between floors with {up} and {down}: each floor has its own chime, and a passenger hums the floor they want. Open the doors with {action} when you are on it. Carry more than one at a time and you will have to remember them all.
game.elevator.name = The Lift
game.elevator.unit = passengers
game.fighters.desc = Read the tell, block, punish.
game.fighters.help = A one on one fight. Your opponent telegraphs: a high whistle is a high strike, block with up. A low thud is a low sweep, block with down. A metallic ring is a grab, break it with {action}. After a successful block, hit back with A for a jab or L for a heavy. Heavies hurt more but leave you open. Knock out five fighters in a row, each tougher and quicker than the last, to win; you get some health back between fights.
game.fighters.name = Fighters
game.fighters.unit = points
game.fire.desc = Put it out before it spreads.
game.fire.help = Fires crackle around you in a ring. Turn with {left} and {right} to face one and hold {action} to hose it. A fire you ignore grows louder and spreads to its neighbours. Put them all out.
game.fire.name = Firefighter
game.fire.unit = points
game.fireeater.desc = Breathe in. Hold. Blow on the beat.
game.fireeater.help = Three stages. A rising hiss means breathe in: hold {action}. When the hiss stops, release. Then a drum roll builds, and you press {action} again exactly when it stops for the flame. Miss the moment and you singe your moustache.
game.fireeater.name = Fire Eater
game.fireeater.unit = flames
game.fireflies.desc = Fireflies blink across the field. Move the jar under one and catch it.
game.fireflies.help = A summer night, and fireflies blink all across the field, each with a soft chirp from where it is. A firefly blinks three times, then flies away. Move your jar with {left} and {right}: a tick comes from where the jar is. Press {action} while a firefly is blinking right over your jar to catch it; a catch on its first blink scores most. Missing costs nothing but time. In Hardcore, moths come too, with a dusty flutter: do not catch those. Ninety seconds.
game.fireflies.name = Firefly Jar
game.fireflies.unit = points
game.fishing.desc = Sonar fishing in the dark.
game.fishing.help = Fish swim past in the stereo field. Move your hook with {left} and {right}, and press {action} when the hook is on top of a fish. Deep rumbles are big fish worth a lot. Ping with {confirm} if you lose track. Sixty seconds.
game.fishing.name = Deep Listen
game.fishing.unit = points
game.fivedice.desc = Roll five dice up to three times a turn and fill thirteen boxes.
game.fivedice.help = A dice game of thirteen turns. Each turn you roll five dice, read out after each roll, up to three times: press {confirm} to roll, and the keys one to five to keep or free each die between rolls; or move along the dice with {left} and {right} and press {action}. {down} switches between the dice and the boxes. Then score the dice in one of thirteen boxes: the ones to the sixes count those faces; three and four of a kind count all the dice; a full house is twenty-five, a small straight of four thirty, a large straight of five forty, five of a kind fifty, and chance counts everything. Choose a box with {left} and {right} once you are on the boxes, hearing what it would score, and {action} to use it. Each box is used once. Sixty-three or more in the ones to the sixes earns a bonus of thirty-five. {up} reads the dice.
game.fivedice.name = Five Dice
game.fivedice.unit = points
game.flappy.desc = Flap through gaps you can only hear.
game.flappy.help = A tone follows your altitude: high pitch means you are high. Tap space to flap upward, gravity does the rest. Walls approach with a whoosh; the gap in each wall hums at its own pitch. Match your pitch to the gap's pitch before you arrive.
game.flappy.name = Flappy Tone
game.flappy.unit = walls
game.forklift.desc = Fetch the pallet. Mind the racking.
game.forklift.help = A pallet beeps somewhere in the warehouse. Drive to it with the four arrows and press {action} to lift, then take it to the loading bay, which hums low and steady. Racking creaks as you get close to it, and clipping one costs you time.
game.forklift.name = Forklift
game.forklift.unit = pallets
game.fourrow.desc = Four of yours in a line before the rival gets four of theirs.
game.fourrow.help = Seven columns stand from your left to your right, six places high. You and a rival take turns dropping a piece into a column; it falls to the lowest free place. Four of your pieces in a line, across, up or on a slant, wins the game. Choose a column with its number, or move along with {left} and {right} and drop with {action}. Every place has its own pitch, higher up the column, and your pieces and the rival's sound different. Press {confirm} to hear the column you are on, from the bottom up. Win for points, lose three games and it is over. In Hardcore the rival thinks further ahead.
game.fourrow.name = Four in a Row
game.fourrow.unit = points
game.freethrow.desc = Hear the hoop, set your aim, judge the arc.
game.freethrow.help = Fifteen shots at a hoop that calls from where it is: the higher its call, the further away it is. Aim with {left} and {right}: a click comes from where you aim, and a bright ping when you are lined up. Hold {action} and a power tone rises; let go to shoot. Too soft falls short, too hard bounces off the back of the rim. A basket scores two, three from beyond the arc, and a clean swish one more. Hardcore spreads the hoop wider and allows less error.
game.freethrow.name = Free Throws
game.freethrow.unit = points
game.frisbee.desc = Line up, wait, and catch.
game.frisbee.help = Frisbees fly along the beach towards you. Move {left} and {right} to line yourself up with one, then press {action} at the moment it arrives to catch it. Time it wrong and it sails past. Later on some come in far too fast to catch, and those you should simply let go.
game.frisbee.name = Frisbee Beach
game.frisbee.unit = catches
game.gaplength.desc = Which silence lasted longer?
game.gaplength.help = Two silences, each marked by a click at its start and end. Press {left} if the first was longer, {right} if the second was. Judging an empty space is harder than judging a sound, which is exactly the point.
game.gaplength.name = Mind The Gap
game.gaplength.unit = correct
game.gators.desc = Five lanes, hungry gators, and a frenzy for the best.
game.gators.help = Five lanes lie in front of you, seven in Hardcore. Walk between them with {left} and {right}, or jump straight to one with its number. Gators creep out along the lanes, each growling from its own lane, quiet at first and louder as it comes closer. Press {action} to bop the gator in your lane: the sooner you bop it, the more it scores, and it slides back with a falling sound. Let one reach you and it chomps, costing points, and swinging at an empty lane costs a little too. They come one at a time at first, then two, then three. Score a thousand points in fifty seconds, thirteen hundred in Hardcore, and the gators get angry: ten more seconds of them coming two and three at once, much faster.
game.gators.name = Gator Bop
game.gators.unit = points
game.gems3.desc = Swap ringing gems to line up three or more of a kind.
game.gems3.help = A six by six board of gems, each kind with its own note and voice, from the low bell to the high chime. Move with {dirs}: each gem rings as you land on it, panned to its column. Press {action} to pick up the gem you are on, then a direction to swap it with its neighbour. A swap only stays if it lines up three or more of a kind, in a row or a column; they ring out together and the gems above fall into the gap, sometimes setting off a chain worth more each time. Press {confirm} for a hint, which costs a few points, and {status} to hear your place and the gem's name. Reach each target to move up a level before the time runs out.
game.gems3.name = Gem Chimes
game.gems3.unit = points
game.ghost.desc = Eat the dots, dodge the growl.
game.ghost.help = A maze full of dots. Arrow keys move. Space echolocates: a click from each wall, louder the closer it is; enter reads out how far each way is open. Dots chime as you take them. A ghost hunts you: it growls with every step it takes, panning and rising as it closes. The maze has loops, so there is always another way round, and now and then the ghost gives up the chase for a few seconds and wanders off to its corner. Grab a power pill, marked by a deep gong, and for a few seconds the ghost flees and you can eat it: an eaten ghost is gone for four seconds, then comes back in the corner furthest from you.
game.ghost.name = Ghost Chase
game.ghost.unit = dots
game.ghosttrain.desc = Something is in the carriage with you.
game.ghosttrain.help = You are riding through the dark. Things lunge at you from the sides: duck with {down} when something swings low, and lean with {left} or {right} away from whatever is reaching for you. A low thud means it is behind you. Survive to the end of the ride.
game.ghosttrain.name = Ghost Train
game.ghosttrain.unit = metres
game.golf.desc = Six holes by ear, from tee to cup.
game.golf.help = Six holes. Before every stroke you face the flag, and the distance to it is read out with the club you will use. Wind and the slope push the ball aside, so aim off with {left} and {right}: the flag calls from where it is compared with your aim, and a bright lock ping marks the aim that allows for them. Then hold {action} for power and let go: full power is the club's full distance, so judge how much you need. On the green you putt, and the ball must finish within a step of the cup to drop. Each hole has a par; every stroke under par scores more, every stroke over less, and eight strokes picks the ball up. Press {confirm} to hear the distance again. Hardcore has stronger wind.
game.golf.name = Golf
game.golf.unit = points
game.gomoko.desc = Five in a row on a nine by nine board, against the computer.
game.gomoko.help = Gomoko, five in a row. The board is nine squares by nine. Move around it with the arrow keys: each square's row and column are read out with what is on it, and a tone sounds from across the board, low at the bottom and high at the top. Press {action} to place a stone. The computer then places one of its own. Five of yours in a line, across, down or diagonally, wins. Press {confirm} to hear where the computer's last stone went. Three games.
game.gomoko.name = Gomoko
game.gomoko.unit = points
game.gridiron.desc = Call the play, find the open man, and march down the field.
game.gridiron.help = American football: you have the ball for eight drives against a computer defence. Each play, choose a run with {down}, or a pass with {up}. On a run, the line opens a hole with a whistle on the left or the right: burst through it with {left} or {right} straight away. On a pass, three receivers run their routes; a covered man may call once, but the open one calls twice, from his side: throw to him with {left}, {action} for the middle, or {right}, before the pass rush gets you. You have four downs to gain ten yards; reach the end zone for a touchdown, worth seven. If you are stopped, the drive ends.
game.gridiron.name = Gridiron
game.gridiron.unit = points
game.guessnum.desc = Higher? Lower? Close in on the secret number.
game.guessnum.help = A secret number hides between one and a thousand, ten thousand in Hardcore. Type your guess with the number keys and press {confirm}, or set it with {up} and {down}: {left} and {right} choose whether they move it by ones, tens, hundreds or thousands. After each guess a rising tone means the number is higher, a falling tone means lower. Find it within ten guesses, fourteen in Hardcore; the fewer you need, the more it scores. Three numbers not found and the game is over.
game.guessnum.name = Guess the Number
game.guessnum.unit = points
game.hammer.desc = Wind up and hit it dead on.
game.hammer.help = The fairground hammer. Hold {action} to wind up: the tone rises as your swing charges, and it peaks right before it overloads. Release at the peak for a full-power hit. Go too far and you fumble it. Ring the bell to move up a weight class.
game.hammer.name = High Striker
game.hammer.unit = points
game.hammer2.desc = Swing the hammer round, faster each turn, and let it fly.
game.hammer2.help = Three throws. The hammer whooshes round you in a circle, and you hear it pass from side to side. Each time it sweeps past in front of you, marked by a click, press {action} to pull and it spins faster, with the whoosh rising. After four good pulls, or up to six for the longest throws, press {confirm} as it passes in front to let it go. A pull or a release off the click wastes speed or sends the throw wide, and a throw that goes wide of the sector is a foul. Your best throw, in metres, scores ten points a metre.
game.hammer2.name = Hammer Throw
game.hammer2.unit = points
game.hammurabi.desc = Rule ancient Sumeria for ten years: land, grain and people.
game.hammurabi.help = You govern the city of Sumeria for a ten-year term. Each year your steward reports: the people, the land, the harvest, and the grain the rats ate. Then you decide four things, typing a number with the digit keys and pressing {confirm}: how many acres of land to buy, how many to sell, how many bushels of grain to feed your people, and how many acres to plant. {up} and {down} add or take ten, {right} and {left} a hundred, and {action} repeats the question with the figures you need. Each person eats twenty bushels a year; planting takes half a bushel of seed an acre, and each person can tend ten acres. Starve too many and you are thrown out. A full term with a growing, well-fed city scores most.
game.hammurabi.name = Hammurabi
game.hammurabi.unit = points
game.handbells.desc = Hear the tune once, then ring your two bells in their places.
game.handbells.help = You are in a handbell choir, holding two bells: a low one in your left hand and a high one in your right. Each round, the choir plays a short tune once with every bell, yours included; your bells have a brighter, ringing sound. Then the tune plays again with your notes left out: ring them on the beat, the low bell with {left} and the high one with {right}. A ring right on the beat scores most. The wrong bell, a ring in the wrong place or a missed note all count against you; ten misses end the concert. Eight rounds, longer and quicker as you go.
game.handbells.name = Handbells
game.handbells.unit = points
game.harmonics.desc = One note in the chord is out.
game.harmonics.help = A chord holds steady and one of its three notes is out of tune. Press one, two or three for the lowest, middle or highest to say which. Press zero to hear it again.
game.harmonics.name = Find The Sour Note
game.harmonics.unit = correct
game.hexapawn.desc = Three pawns each on a tiny board, against a rival that learns.
game.hexapawn.help = Hexapawn, on a board three squares by three. Your three pawns start on the near row, the computer's on the far row. A pawn moves one square straight ahead into an empty square, or one square diagonally ahead to take an enemy pawn. You win by reaching the far row, taking every enemy pawn, or leaving the computer with no move. {left} and {right} go through your possible moves, read out, and {action} makes one. {up} reads the board. Nine games. The computer starts out careless, but it learns from every game it loses, and never makes a losing move twice.
game.hexapawn.name = Hexapawn
game.hexapawn.unit = points
game.highdive.desc = Let go at the top of the bounce.
game.highdive.help = You bounce on a board, and the tone rises as you rise. Press {action} at the very top of a bounce to launch. The higher you launch, the better the dive scores, but leave it too late and you have already started falling. Ten dives in a session.
game.highdive.name = High Dive
game.highdive.unit = dives
game.highjump.desc = Run up in rhythm, take off on the mark.
game.highjump.help = Run up to the bar with {left} and {right}, one after the other: every stride is a footstep, and the faster your strides, the higher you can clear. Pressing the same key twice stumbles. After ten strides a chime marks the take-off: press {up} right on it. Clear the bar and it goes up five centimetres; three failures at one height and the competition is over. Higher bars need a quicker run-up. Hardcore starts higher with a tighter take-off.
game.highjump.name = High Jump
game.highjump.unit = points
game.highlow.desc = Two tones ring. Which came more often?
game.highlow.help = A burst of beeps plays, some high and some low, mixed together. Track both: were there more HIGH beeps or more LOW ones? Press {left} if high won, {right} if low won. They come faster as you go. Three wrong ends it.
game.highlow.name = High Or Low Count
game.highlow.unit = correct
game.hockey.desc = Block the puck, then bury it.
game.hockey.help = The puck slides across the table. Move your mallet with {left} and {right}; press {action} to smack it hard when it is near you. The puck clicks where it is and rises in pitch as it comes back to your end. Five goals wins.
game.hockey.name = Air Hockey
game.hockey.unit = goals
game.homerun.desc = Read the pitch, swing on the pop, and send it over the fence.
game.homerun.help = You bat in a home run derby until you make ten outs. The pitcher winds up, and the ball whistles toward you: a fastball comes in quick and high, a changeup slower and lower, and a curve bends across from one side to the other. Swing with {action} just as the ball reaches you, when its whistle peaks. Right on time is a home run; a little off is a hit or a foul; badly off is a miss. A pitch that sounds wide, far off to one side, is a ball: let it go. Swinging at a ball, a miss, a foul or a caught fly all cost an out; a hit that is not a home run costs nothing. Ten outs, or thirty pitches, and the derby is over.
game.homerun.name = Home Run Derby
game.homerun.unit = points
game.hoopla.desc = Ring the prize. Mind the swing.
game.hoopla.help = A prize hums in front of you and your throwing arm swings {left} and {right} on its own. The prize moves to the centre of your hearing when your arm is lined up with it. Release with {action} at that moment. The swing speeds up each time you score.
game.hoopla.name = Hoopla
game.hoopla.unit = rings
game.hotpotato.desc = Catch it, hear who is calling, throw it on. Before it bursts.
game.hotpotato.help = Three friends stand around you: one on your left, one in front and one on your right. The potato lands in your hands with a thump and its fuse starts to tick. Listen for which friend claps for it, and throw it to them: {left}, {up} or {right}. The quicker the throw, the more it scores. A throw to the wrong friend is dropped and costs you one of three chances, and so does holding it when the fuse runs out: the ticking speeds up as it gets close. Make forty good throws to win. In Hardcore a friend may cough instead of clapping: do not throw to them.
game.hotpotato.name = Hot Potato
game.hotpotato.unit = points
game.hurdles.desc = Sprint, and time the leap over ten hurdles.
game.hurdles.help = Two races over a hundred and ten metres and ten hurdles, against three rivals in the lanes beside you. On your marks, set, then the gun: press {left} and {right} one after the other to run; the same key twice stumbles, and a press before the gun is a false start. As each hurdle comes near, a knock sounds, faster and louder the closer it is: press {up} to leap when the knocks run together. Too early or too late and you clip it and lose speed; not at all and you fall through it. A clean race and a quick time score most, and a win scores a bonus. Hardcore leaves less room for the leap.
game.hurdles.name = 110 Metres Hurdles
game.hurdles.unit = points
game.hurkle.desc = A hurkle hides on a ten by ten grid. Five guesses to find it.
game.hurkle.help = A happy little hurkle hides somewhere on a grid ten squares by ten, numbered nought to nine across and nought to nine up. Move your search spot with the arrow keys, and each square's numbers are read out, or type two digits, across then up. Press {action} to look there. If the hurkle is not there, you are told which way to go, north, south, east, west or between, and a tone comes from that direction: higher for north, lower for south. You have five looks for each hurkle; six hurkles in all. The fewer looks, the more it scores.
game.hurkle.name = Hunt the Hurkle
game.hurkle.unit = points
game.icehockey.desc = Skate past the defender, beat the goalie, then stop their rush.
game.icehockey.help = Three periods of ice hockey, attacking and defending in turn. In attack, a defender skates at you, his blades scraping from where he is: as the scrape gets loud, swerve to the other side with {left} or {right} to get past him. Then the goalie shuffles from side to side in front of the net: shoot with {left} or {right} into the side he is not on. In defence, their forward taps the puck as he skates down the ice: stay on him with {left} and {right}, and when he is right in front of you, a ping, press {action} to poke the puck away before he shoots. Each period has four attacks and four defences.
game.icehockey.name = Ice Hockey
game.icehockey.unit = points
game.intervals.desc = How far apart were those two notes?
game.intervals.help = Two notes play in turn. Press the interval's own number: two for a second, three for a third, four for a fourth, five for a fifth, and eight for an octave. Press zero to hear them again.
game.intervals.name = Interval Trainer
game.intervals.unit = correct
game.invaders.desc = Know each ship by ear, and pick the right weapon. After Oriol Gomez's Space Invaders.
game.invaders.help = You hold the centre of space, and ships come at you from far off, each heard from where it is and pulsing faster as it nears. Sweep your crosshair across with {left} and {right}; when a ship is under it, a lock tone sounds in that ship's own voice. Scouts buzz high, bombers hum softly, battleships growl low, and civilian freighters chime gently: do not shoot them. Key 1 fires the pulse, right against scouts; key 2 the beam, right against bombers; key 3 the missile, right against battleships; {action} fires the weapon you last used. The right weapon scores most; the wrong one still destroys a ship for less; the third bounces off. Each shot costs energy, which comes back by itself. Right-weapon kills in a row multiply your score. A warship that reaches you, or a civilian you shoot, costs one of three lives. Each wave brings new ships and weapons; more lives at twenty thousand points and beyond. Hardcore ships are faster. After Space Invaders by Oriol Gomez.
game.invaders.name = Space Invaders
game.invaders.unit = points
game.joust.desc = Meet them high, not low.
game.joust.help = You and a rival fly toward each other. Tap space to gain height and let go to sink. Whoever is higher at the moment you meet wins the pass. A rising whoosh means they are climbing, a falling one means they are dropping.
game.joust.name = Joust
game.joust.unit = passes
game.juggler.desc = Keep every ball in the air, catching each one as it comes down.
game.juggler.help = You juggle balls, each with its own key and its own place: {k1} far left, {k2} left, {k3} right and {k4} far right. A ball whistles from its place as it flies, falling in pitch as it comes down; a tick says it is in your hand's reach. Press its key then to throw it up again. Too early and it slips, too late and it drops. Every catch scores, more balls join as you go, and three drops end the act.
game.juggler.name = Juggler
game.juggler.unit = points
game.keycutter.desc = Hear the key, then cut its twin.
game.keycutter.help = A customer's key has five notches, each one cut to a height from one to five, and every height has its own tone: the higher the notch, the higher the tone. Press {confirm} to hear their key, notch by notch. Your blank starts with every notch at height one. {left} and {right} move along your blank, and {up} and {down} cut a notch higher or lower; each notch plays as you touch it. Press {action} to hear your whole key, and {confirm} twice quickly to try it in the lock. A wrong key tells you how many notches are wrong. Three wrong keys and the shift is over. In Hardcore keys have six notches and you may hear the customer's key only twice more after it is handed to you.
game.keycutter.name = Key Cutter
game.keycutter.unit = points
game.kinema.desc = A ball thrown upward: how high, how long, how fast?
game.kinema.help = A ball is thrown straight up at a speed in metres a second. Three questions follow: how high it goes, in metres; how long until it comes back down, in seconds; and how fast it is moving after a number of seconds, where a ball on its way down has a negative speed, so press the minus key for a minus sign. Take gravity as ten. Type your answer and press {confirm}; within fifteen percent is close enough, rounding allowed. {action} hears the question again. Six balls.
game.kinema.name = Kinema
game.kinema.unit = points
game.kitchen.desc = Three pans, three timers, one pair of hands.
game.kitchen.help = Three pans cook at once, one on each of the keys A, S and D; Hardcore adds a fourth on F. Each sizzles while it cooks and rings when it is ready. Press its key the moment it rings. Leave it and it burns, and a burning pan smells worse than it sounds.
game.kitchen.name = Night Kitchen
game.kitchen.unit = dishes
game.knight.desc = Move a chess knight to each flag in as few jumps as you can.
game.knight.help = You are a knight on a board of six by six, moving as a knight does: two squares one way and one the other. {left} and {right} go through the jumps open to you, each said as the square it lands on, and {action} makes the jump. A flag rings from where it is; reach it to score, more if you take no more jumps than you need. Press {confirm} for where you and the flag are. Ten flags, against the clock.
game.knight.name = Knight's Path
game.knight.unit = points
game.labyrinth.desc = A bigger maze, and a clock.
game.labyrinth.help = A large maze with a timer. Arrows move, space echolocates, and the exit hums from its direction. Keys are scattered around: you need all of them before the exit will open, and each one you collect buys more time.
game.labyrinth.name = Labyrinth
game.labyrinth.unit = points
game.ladder.desc = Put the three sounds in order.
game.ladder.help = Three sounds play, numbered one, two and three from left to right. Press their numbers in order from quietest to loudest. Press zero to hear them again.
game.ladder.name = Loudness Ladder
game.ladder.unit = correct
game.lander.desc = Land softly, or become a crater.
game.lander.help = You are falling. Hold {action} to fire the thruster. A descending tone tracks your altitude and a click track ticks faster the faster you are falling. Touch down under one metre per second. Fuel is limited and the thruster roars while it burns.
game.lander.name = Lunar Lander
game.lander.unit = points
game.laserrun.desc = A high hum means duck, a low one means jump. Sixty beams.
game.laserrun.help = You sprint down a corridor of laser beams. Each beam hums as it comes toward you, louder the closer it is: a high hum is a beam at head height, so duck under it with {down}; a low hum is at your ankles, so jump it with {up}. Move just before it reaches you, when the hum is loudest: too early and you are back on your feet when it arrives. A wrong move or none at all and it zaps you; three zaps end the run. Clear sixty beams to finish. A streak of clean beams scores more, and the beams come faster as you go.
game.laserrun.name = Laser Run
game.laserrun.unit = points
game.lastorders.desc = Four bars, a queue of thirsty regulars, and drinks to slide.
game.lastorders.help = You run four bars, each with its own bell note, from low at the front to high at the back. Move between them with {up} and {down}. Customers come in at the far end of a bar and walk toward you: their bell rings at that bar's note, faster and louder as they come close. Press {action} to slide a drink down the bar you are at; it reaches the nearest customer on it, who drinks and leaves happy. If a customer reaches your end, they storm out and you lose one of three chances. A drink down an empty bar smashes at the end and costs points. Serve forty customers to close up for the night.
game.lastorders.name = Last Orders
game.lastorders.unit = points
game.launch.desc = Straight up, whatever the wind says.
game.launch.help = The autopilot is broken: fly the rocket up by hand. The engine is heard from where the rocket is pointing: straight ahead means right on course. Gusts keep pushing it aside; steer back with {left} and {right}. The straighter you fly, the faster you climb, and the engine rises in pitch as you speed up. A warning beeps when you stray too far, and if you stay out there the rocket is lost. You have three rockets. Your score is how high you get. In Hardcore the gusts are stronger and the safe cone is narrower.
game.launch.name = Launch Control
game.launch.unit = points
game.letters.desc = Each letter is a number. The clues tell you which.
game.letters.help = Each letter stands for a number, every letter a different one. Clues are read out, such as A plus A is eight, and B is A plus three. Work the letters out in turn: when asked for a letter, type its number and press {confirm}; minus makes it negative. Once you have found a letter, the clues say its number instead. {action} hears the clues again. Solve every letter for a bonus. The puzzles grow harder as you go: more letters, times as well as plus and minus, then numbers below nought, and clues that point back further and come in any order. A wrong number or running out of time costs one of three lives. Hardcore starts with the harder puzzles.
game.letters.name = Letter Sums
game.letters.unit = correct
game.lightcycles.desc = Ride a grid that fills with walls. Make the rival crash first.
game.lightcycles.help = You and a rival ride light cycles on a square grid, each leaving a wall behind. You always move forward; turn left with {left} and right with {right}. Your radar pings three ways at every step: ahead in the middle, to your left and to your right, each higher and louder the closer the nearest wall that way. The rival's engine hums from where it is around you. Crash into any wall, the grid's edge or a trail, and you lose the round; make the rival crash first and you win it. Five rounds.
game.lightcycles.name = Light Cycles
game.lightcycles.unit = points
game.lighthouse.desc = Swing the beam onto the ship in trouble.
game.lighthouse.help = Ships call out of the dark all around you. Turn the lamp with {left} and {right} until a caller is directly ahead, then hold {action} to hold the beam on it until it is safe. A low double thud means the ship is behind you.
game.lighthouse.name = Lighthouse
game.lighthouse.unit = ships
game.lightsout.desc = Switch off every light, though each switch flips its neighbours too.
game.lightsout.help = A grid of lights, four by four at first and five by five from the fourth board. Move with {dirs}: a lit square rings bright, a dark one gives a soft low tick. Press {action} to flip the square you are on, which also flips the squares above, below, left and right of it. Press {confirm} to hear how many lights are still on and the row you are on as rings and ticks, and {status} for your place. Switch every light off to clear the board: the fewer flips, the more points.
game.lightsout.name = Lights Out
game.lightsout.unit = points
game.lockpick.desc = Lift each pin to the faint click of its set point, and open the lock.
game.lockpick.help = A lock of pins, three at first and up to six. Hold {up} to lift the pin you are on: a tone rises as it goes up, and at its set point there is a faint click. Let go right there to set the pin, with a firm clunk. Lift too far and the pin overshoots: every pin falls back down and you start again. Set them all, from left to right, to open the lock before its time runs out. Press {status} to hear which pin you are on.
game.lockpick.name = Lock Picker
game.lockpick.unit = points
game.locksmith.desc = Feel for the click in each pin.
game.locksmith.help = A lock with several pins. Move the pick up and down with {up} and {down}: as you approach a pin's setting the scraping narrows to a click. Press {action} on the click to set that pin, then move to the next. Set them all before the lock resets.
game.locksmith.name = Locksmith
game.locksmith.unit = locks
game.longjump.desc = Sprint down the runway and leap from the board.
game.longjump.help = Three jumps down the runway. Press {left} and {right} one after the other to build speed. The take-off board beeps as you come towards it, faster and higher as it gets close; press {up} to jump as the beeps run together into one long tone. Jump too early and you lose distance, too late and you overstep the board, which is a foul. The faster your run and the closer to the board you take off, the longer the jump. Your best jump, in centimetres, is your score.
game.longjump.name = Long Jump
game.longjump.unit = points
game.loudness.desc = Which of those was louder?
game.loudness.help = Two sounds play, one after the other. Press left if the first was louder, right if the second was. They get closer together as you go. Press {confirm} to hear the pair again.
game.loudness.name = Loudest Wins
game.loudness.unit = correct
game.maketen.desc = What makes it up to ten? Then twenty, then a hundred.
game.maketen.help = A number is read out, with the total to make: type the number that makes it up to that total and press {confirm}. It starts with ten, then twenty, then a hundred as you go. Backspace corrects, {up} and {down} change the number one at a time, and {action} hears the question again. The faster, the more it scores; a wrong answer or running out of time costs one of three lives. In Hardcore it starts at twenty and there is less time.
game.maketen.name = Make Ten
game.maketen.unit = correct
game.marble.desc = Tilt the table, thread the holes.
game.marble.help = A marble rolls on a tilting table. Hold left or right to tilt. The marble rumbles where it is and how fast it rolls. Shutters in the floor open and close: an open one hisses and will swallow you, a shut one clunks and is safe to cross. Time your run and reach the chime on the far right.
game.marble.name = Marble Run
game.marble.unit = points
game.mathladder.desc = Every right answer is a rung up. How high can you climb?
game.mathladder.help = Climb the ladder one right answer at a time. Each rung asks a question, adding, taking away, times or halving, and the questions get harder and the clock shorter as you climb; the rung you reach is played as a rising note. Type the answer and press {confirm}; {action} hears it again. A wrong answer or running out of time drops you three rungs and costs one of three lives. Your score grows with every rung, more the higher you are. In Hardcore a slip drops you five rungs.
game.mathladder.name = Math Ladder
game.mathladder.unit = correct
game.mathstar.desc = Sums on the beat. After Oriol Gomez's Mathstar.
game.mathstar.help = A groove plays. Each level begins with a bar of count-in; then a sum is read out and you type the answer, digit by digit, before its two bars of music run out (four bars from level ten). Each digit sounds its own note, so every answer is a little tune, and the answer is taken as soon as it is complete. The first wrong digit ends that sum and costs one of three lives, and so does running out of time; a bar's rest follows. Clear enough sums and the level goes up: the tempo rises, the key changes, and the sums grow harder, from adding to taking away, times, and from level eight dividing. Quick answers and harder sums score more. Hardcore starts at level five. The round lasts five minutes. After Mathstar by Oriol Gomez.
game.mathstar.name = Math Star
game.mathstar.unit = points
game.maze.desc = Find the exit in total darkness.
game.maze.help = Move with {dirs} through a grid maze. Press {action} to echolocate: four pings tell you how far the walls are to the north, south, west and east. The exit hums constantly, panned and pitched towards its direction. Walls hurt your score.
game.maze.name = Echo Maze
game.maze.unit = points
game.memory.desc = Repeat the growing melody.
game.memory.help = Listen to the melody, then play it back. The number keys one to four also work as the pads. Four pads: A and S on the left, K and L on the right, each with its own pitch. The melody grows by one note every round.
game.memory.name = Memory Maestro
game.memory.unit = notes
game.merge.desc = Drop tones together to grow them.
game.merge.help = Drop a ball into one of six columns with the number keys. When two balls of the same pitch meet in a column they merge into one an octave higher. Space reads the columns. Fill a column to the top and it is over.
game.merge.name = Ball Merge
game.merge.unit = points
game.meteors.desc = Dodge meteors whistling down five lanes, and catch the falling stars.
game.meteors.help = You stand on the ground in one of five lanes, moving with {left} and {right}. Meteors fall, each whistling down in pitch from its lane: when its whistle is low it is about to land. Be out of its lane by then. Falling stars twinkle instead: be in their lane to catch them for points. The shower thickens as it goes; three hits and it is over.
game.meteors.name = Meteor Shower
game.meteors.unit = points
game.metronome.desc = Match the speed you were given.
game.metronome.help = A tempo plays, then stops. Set your own metronome to the same speed with {up} for faster and {down} for slower, then press {action} when it matches. Yours ticks the whole time so you can compare.
game.metronome.name = Set The Tempo
game.metronome.unit = matched
game.minesweeper.desc = Clear the minefield by working out where the mines must be.
game.minesweeper.help = A field of hidden squares hides a few mines. Walk it with {dirs}: a hidden square gives a soft tap, a flagged one a low knock. Press {action} to dig. A dug square says how many mines touch it and ticks that many times; a square with none opens all its neighbours by itself. Press {confirm} to flag a square you are sure hides a mine. Press {status} to hear where you are. Clear every safe square to finish the field; dig a mine and you lose a life. Your first dig is always safe.
game.minesweeper.name = Minesweeper
game.minesweeper.unit = points
game.mining.desc = Grab the ore, dodge the rock.
game.mining.help = Ore chimes and loose rock rumbles, both drifting past you. Move with {dirs}: catch the chimes, avoid the rumbles. Everything is placed around you, so a low thud means it is behind you and you should turn around.
game.mining.name = Asteroid Mine
game.mining.unit = ore
game.mirrorimage.desc = Put the twin exactly where the mirror says.
game.mirrorimage.help = A sound plays from one side of you. Your own sound starts in the middle: move it with {left} and {right}, and it plays where it now is. Place it at the exact mirror image of the first, just as far out on the other side, and press {confirm}. The closer, the more it scores. Press {action} to hear the first sound again, not in Hardcore. Three placements too far out and the game is over.
game.mirrorimage.name = Mirror Image
game.mirrorimage.unit = points
game.mirrors.desc = Find the real voice among the echoes.
game.mirrors.help = A voice calls from somewhere in the hall, and the mirrors throw back copies of it from the wrong places. Every call, the real voice sounds first: one smooth, long, pure note. Then each mirror answers from its own direction with a short, buzzy double tap. Ignore the double taps and walk toward the long note with {dirs}; it grows louder and clearer as you get close. Press {action} when you are standing on it.
game.mirrors.name = Hall of Mirrors
game.mirrors.unit = found
game.missile.desc = Six cities, three batteries, and the whole sky. After Oriol Gomez's Missile Command.
game.missile.help = Six cities stand along the ground, from left to right, with a missile battery at each end and one in the middle. Move your crosshair anywhere in the sky with {dirs}: a soft ping rises as you aim higher, and a lock tone swells as the crosshair nears a threat, wobbling when the lock is perfect. Z, X and C fire from the left, centre and right batteries, each with its own thunk; {action} fires from the nearest battery with missiles left. A shot whistles up to the crosshair and bursts into a cloud that destroys whatever flies into it. Incoming missiles whistle as they fall, louder as they near the ground; splitters divide on the way down, and bombers drone across the sky dropping bombs. Each wave brings more and faster threats; what is left of your missiles and cities scores a bonus, and every ten thousand points rebuilds a lost city. Lose all six and the game is over. Hardcore starts at wave three. After Missile Command by Oriol Gomez.
game.missile.name = Missile Command
game.missile.unit = points
game.missing.desc = Something plus what makes fifteen?
game.missing.help = A sum is read out with one number missing: type the missing number and press {confirm}. Seven plus what makes fifteen? Eight. {action} hears it again. The faster, the more it scores; a wrong number or running out of time costs one of three lives. In Hardcore there are divisions too, and bigger numbers.
game.missing.name = Missing Number
game.missing.unit = correct
game.mugwump.desc = Four mugwumps hide on a grid. Each guess tells you how far each one is.
game.mugwump.help = Four mugwumps hide on a grid ten squares by ten, numbered nought to nine across and nought to nine up. Type two digits, across then up, or move your spot with the arrow keys, and press {action} to look there. You are told how far you are from each mugwump still hiding, in squares as the crow flies, rounded to a tenth. Find all four in ten looks. Five hunts; the fewer looks, the more you score.
game.mugwump.name = Mugwump
game.mugwump.unit = points
game.nail.desc = Drive it flush. Not one blow too hard.
game.nail.help = You and a rival take turns hitting a nail. The nail sticks out a number of millimetres, read out and heard as a tone that rises as it gets closer to flush. On your turn press one for a light tap, which always drives it one millimetre; two for a firm blow, one to three millimetres; or three for a heavy blow, two to five. Whoever drives it exactly flush wins the round, but a blow that would go past flush bends the nail and hands the round to the other player. Lose three rounds and the match is over. In Hardcore your rival never makes a careless blow.
game.nail.name = The Nail
game.nail.unit = points
game.neverstop.desc = Keep moving. The floor is disappearing.
game.neverstop.help = You are running along a corridor that collapses behind you. Press {action} in rhythm to keep running: each press carries you forward, and the corridor eats the ground if you pause. Gaps whistle ahead of you: jump them with up. It only gets faster.
game.neverstop.name = Never Stop
game.neverstop.unit = metres
game.nightbus.desc = Call the stop before you reach it.
game.nightbus.help = The bus runs its route. Each stop is announced by a landmark sound as you approach it, and you must call the stop with {action} while that sound is still playing. Call too early or too late and somebody misses their stop.
game.nightbus.name = Night Bus
game.nightbus.unit = stops
game.nightradio.desc = Keep the music going and take the listeners' calls.
game.nightradio.help = You are on air through the night. A song plays, and as it ends it fades away: press {action} to start the next one while it is fading, for a smooth change. Too early cuts the song short; too late leaves dead air, a hiss that costs points every second until you start the next song. Now and then the phone rings: press {up} to take the listener's call before the third ring. Sometimes a chime tells you an advert is due: at the next change press {down} instead of {action} to play it, for the station's money. The shift is fifteen songs.
game.nightradio.name = Night Radio
game.nightradio.unit = points
game.nightwatch.desc = Something is moving in the building.
game.nightwatch.help = You are on patrol. Most of what you hear is the building settling. One sound is somebody who should not be here. The four arrows walk you around: {up} north, {down} south, {left} west, {right} east. Press {action} when you are on them. A low double thud means a sound is behind you.
game.nightwatch.name = Night Watch
game.nightwatch.unit = caught
game.notehold.desc = Hold the key for exactly as long as the tone lasted.
game.notehold.help = A tone sounds for a certain length. Hold {action} for the same length and release. Not the rhythm, the duration. Your own note plays while you hold it so you can feel the length.
game.notehold.name = Hold That Note
game.notehold.unit = correct
game.numline.desc = Where on the line is that tone? Name the number.
game.numline.help = A number line runs from nought on your left to a hundred on your right, rising in pitch as it goes. A tone sounds somewhere along it: type the number you think it marks and press {confirm}. Exact scores best, close still scores, and too far out costs one of three lives. {action} plays the tone again, and G plays nought, fifty and a hundred as a guide, then the tone. In Hardcore there is no guide and you must be closer.
game.numline.name = Number Line
game.numline.unit = correct
game.oddduck.desc = One of these ducks does not belong.
game.oddduck.help = A flock of ducks quacks around you. All of them sound alike except one intruder, whose call is subtly different. Turn with {left} and {right}, walk with up, and press {action} when you are on top of the one you think is the stranger. Get it wrong and the flock scatters and reforms.
game.oddduck.name = Odd Duck
game.oddduck.unit = caught
game.oddeven.desc = Count the beeps. Odd or even?
game.oddeven.help = A quick burst of beeps plays. Decide whether there were an odd or an even number, and press {left} for odd, {right} for even. They come faster as you go. Three wrong ends it.
game.oddeven.name = Odd Or Even
game.oddeven.unit = correct
game.oddnum.desc = Every number follows the rule but one.
game.oddnum.help = A few numbers are read out. All of them follow one rule except one: they might all be multiples of the same number, all even, all odd, all square numbers, or go up in equal steps. Type the position of the one that breaks the rule, one for the first, and press {confirm}. {action} hears them again. The faster, the more it scores; a wrong answer or running out of time costs one of three lives. In Hardcore there are more numbers, and primes join the rules.
game.oddnum.name = Odd Number Out
game.oddnum.unit = correct
game.oddone.desc = One of these is not like the others.
game.oddone.help = Three or more sounds play in a row, left to right. All of them match except one, which differs in pitch, in timbre, or in length. Press its number. Once there are ten or more sounds, type two digits for ten and above: one then zero is ten, one then two is twelve, and one on its own is one. You can also walk the row with {left} and {right}, hearing each sound on its own, and press {action} to choose the one you are on. Press zero to hear them all again, except straight after a one, when zero makes ten.
game.oddone.name = Odd One Out
game.oddone.unit = correct
game.orbit.desc = An enemy ship circles your base. Set angle and range, and fire.
game.orbit.help = An enemy ship orbits your base, its engine humming from its direction, all the way round you: in front, to either side, or behind, where it sounds muffled. The higher its hum, the closer it is. Turn your gun with {left} and {right}, by fifteen degrees a step, and set the shell's range with {up} and {down}: a tone tells you the range, matching the ship's pitch when it is right. Press {action} to fire. The shell bursts after a moment, so aim a step ahead of the ship. Five ships, seven shells each.
game.orbit.name = Orbit
game.orbit.unit = points
game.orchestra.desc = Which instrument was that?
game.orchestra.help = A single note plays on one of the arcade's instruments. Press one for a plucked string, two for a bowed string, three for a bell, four for a chip pulse, five for a brass-like tone. Press zero to hear it again. This is timbre training, not pitch.
game.orchestra.name = Name That Voice
game.orchestra.unit = correct
game.pairs.desc = Concentration, played entirely by ear.
game.pairs.help = Six boards to clear, then you are done. A row of cards, each hiding a sound, and every sound appears twice. Move along the row with {left} and {right}, and press {confirm} to turn the card you are on. Cards one to nine also have number keys. Turn two that match and they stay open. Press {action} to hear which cards are still face down, and tab to hear where your cursor is. The decks change from board to board: tones, then spoken numbers, then spoken words, and round again.
game.pairs.name = Sound Pairs
game.pairs.unit = pairs
game.paperroute.desc = Ring-ring: throw the paper to the houses that ordered one.
game.paperroute.help = Ride your bike down a street of thirty houses, on both sides. A house that takes the paper chimes its doorbell as you come near; a house that does not has a dog that barks. Each sound comes from the side the house is on. Throw left with {left} and right with {right} as the house reaches you: the closer you are, the better the throw, and a paper right on the step scores extra. Too early lands in the hedge. A paper at a barking house breaks a window and costs points. Potholes rumble up the middle of the road: hop them with {action}, or come off the bike. Three falls end the round. The street gets faster as you go.
game.paperroute.name = Paper Round
game.paperroute.unit = points
game.parachute.desc = Falling fast. Grab what floats past.
game.parachute.help = You are falling under a parachute. Prizes float in the air around you: drift {left} and {right} to line up with them before they pass. Some are hazards that whistle sharply, and hitting one costs you. The ground is coming up either way.
game.parachute.name = Parachute Drop
game.parachute.unit = points
game.penalty.desc = Five kicks, five saves: read the keeper, then be one.
game.penalty.help = A shootout of five kicks and five saves, in turn. When you take a kick, the keeper shuffles on his line, and you hear which way he leans: pick a corner with {left} or {right}, or {up} for the middle, then press {action} to shoot before time runs out: a short whistle warns you. Shoot away from his lean. When you are in goal, the kicker runs up; the moment he strikes, the ball flies to one side or the middle. Dive with {left} or {right}, or press {up} to stay up, before it gets past you. Diving before the kick guesses blind. A goal or a save scores a hundred, and winning the shootout three hundred more. Hardcore has a sharper keeper and harder kicks.
game.penalty.name = Penalty Shootout
game.penalty.unit = points
game.pinball.desc = Flip on instinct, hunt the bumpers.
game.pinball.help = Each ball waits in the launch lane on your right, ticking softly. Hold {action} to pull back the plunger, a rising tone, and let go to launch: the harder the pull, the higher it flies. The ball rolls around a table you can hear, higher tones higher up the table. Bumpers ring when you hit them. Hold A for the left flipper and L for the right: a flipper hits the ball if it arrives on that side within a moment of your press. Press {up} to nudge the table and push the ball, but nudge three times in a few seconds and the table tilts, losing the ball. Let the ball past the flippers and you lose it. Three balls.
game.pinball.name = Pinball
game.pinball.unit = points
game.pingpong.desc = Toss, serve and rally across the table by ear.
game.pingpong.help = A match against the club player across the table: the first to eleven points, two clear, takes a game, and two games take the match. Serves change every two points. To serve, press {action} to toss the ball: it rises on a climbing tone and falls on a dropping one. Strike as it peaks: {action} serves it forward, fast and hard to return; {down} serves it down into the table, short and safe; {up} serves it high, slow and sure, but it may come back as a smash. In a rally the ball ticks from where it is compared with your bat, and bounces on the table once on each side. Move with {left} and {right} until the ticks are centred, then hit just after it bounces on your side, as the rising hit note sounds: {action} for a drive, {up} for a safe lob, {down} for a smash that is hard to return but easy to send flying. Hold {left} or {right} as you hit to angle the ball away from your rival. Too early, too late or off the edge of the bat and it hits the net or flies off the table. Press {confirm} to hear the score. Hardcore brings a faster rival.
game.pingpong.name = Table Tennis
game.pingpong.unit = points
game.pitch.desc = Higher, lower, or the same?
game.pitch.help = Two tones play in a row. Press up if the second is higher, down if it is lower, space if they are identical. Press {confirm} to hear the pair again as often as you need before you answer. The gap narrows each time you are right. Three wrong answers ends it.
game.pitch.name = Pitch Perfect
game.pitch.unit = correct
game.pitchsort.desc = Low on the left, high on the right.
game.pitchsort.help = A row of tones stands from your left to your right, all mixed up. Put them in order: the lowest on the left, rising to the highest on the right. Move along the row with {left} and {right}; each tone plays as you reach it. Press {action} to pick a tone up, move it with {left} and {right}, and press {action} again to put it down. Press {confirm} when you think the row is in order. Each sorted row adds a tone to the next; a wrong row costs one of three chances. In Hardcore the tones sit closer together.
game.pitchsort.name = Pitch Sort
game.pitchsort.unit = points
game.polyrhythm.desc = Tap two beats at once: three on the left against two on the right.
game.polyrhythm.help = Two drums play at the same time: one on the left, beating three times a bar, and one on the right beating twice, so their beats meet only on the one. After a bar of listening, tap {left} with every left beat and {right} with every right beat. On the one, tap both. Taps on time score, more for the tightest; a beat missed or a tap with nothing there costs you a little of your groove, and when the groove runs out the game ends. The tempo rises, and later bars bring four against three.
game.polyrhythm.name = Polyrhythm
game.polyrhythm.unit = points
game.pong.desc = First to seven, with a swing and power-ups. After Oriol Gomez's Pong.
game.pong.help = You hold your end of a long table, the computer the far end. Move your paddle across the table with {left} and {right}, a step at a time, each step a little higher the further right you are. The ball hums all the time, heard from where it is compared with your paddle and rising in pitch as it comes towards you. Press {action} as it reaches you to swing: a swing hits hard, and where the ball meets your paddle sends it left or right; a ball you do not swing at only bounces back weakly. Press {action} to serve, too, before the warning beeps run out. Now and then a power-up ball rolls across your end of the table, named as it appears: stand in its way to take it. It may widen your paddle, shield you from one goal, strengthen your swing, freeze your opponent, curve your returns or make the walls bouncy; the computer can take its own. First to seven points wins the match. In Hardcore the computer is sharper and power-ups are rarer. After Pong by Oriol Gomez.
game.pong.name = Pong
game.pong.unit = points
game.pool.desc = Numbered balls on a real table: lowest first, any pocket.
game.pool.help = A table of numbered balls, each with its own note, low for the one, higher for each number after it. You play the white from the near end of the table. Turn your cue with {left} and {right}: a short tap turns it a hair, holding turns it faster. {up} and {down} point straight at the next or previous ball. Whatever the cue points at is spoken, and when the cut would send that ball into a pocket a bright lock ping rings and the pocket is named. Hold {action} for power and let go to strike. The balls then roll for real: they knock into each other, each with its own note, bounce off the cushions and drop into the six pockets. The white must hit the lowest numbered ball first; after that any ball that drops counts, two in one shot score extra, and the lowest one going down in order earns a bonus. Hitting another ball first, hitting nothing, or the white dropping is a foul, and the white comes back to the near end. Three fouls in a row end the game; clear the table for a new rack. Press {confirm} to hear the table. Hardcore racks nine balls instead of six.
game.pool.name = Pool
game.pool.unit = points
game.press.desc = Keep it running. Catch the jam early.
game.press.help = The press runs in a steady rhythm. When it slips out of rhythm it is about to jam: press {action} the moment you hear the stumble to clear it. Press when it is running fine and you stop the line for nothing.
game.press.name = Printing Press
game.press.unit = pages
game.primefactor.desc = Name the smallest prime that divides the number.
game.primefactor.help = A number is read out: type the smallest prime number that divides it, and press {confirm}. Backspace corrects, {up} and {down} change the number one at a time, and {action} hears the number again. If the number is itself prime, type the number. Answer before the ticking runs out; a wrong answer or running out of time costs one of three lives. The numbers grow as you go.
game.primefactor.name = Prime Factor
game.primefactor.unit = correct
game.primes.desc = Numbers go by. Catch every prime.
game.primes.help = Numbers are read out one after another. Press {action} on every prime: a number that only divides by one and itself, like two, three, five, seven, eleven and thirteen. Press while the number is the latest one read. Catching a prime scores, and more for every five in a row; pressing on a number that is not prime, or letting a prime go by, costs one of three lives. The numbers grow bigger, up to a hundred, and come faster as you go. In Hardcore they reach two hundred and come faster still.
game.primes.name = Prime Time
game.primes.unit = correct
game.pulsewidth.desc = The same note, shaped three ways.
game.pulsewidth.help = A pulse wave sounds hollow, reedy or nasal depending on its shape. One plays: press one for the full hollow sound, two for the reedy middle, three for the thin nasal one. Press zero to hear it again.
game.pulsewidth.name = Thin Or Fat
game.pulsewidth.unit = correct
game.quickdraw.desc = Fastest finger. Wait for the tone, then fire.
game.quickdraw.help = Keep your finger off the trigger. When you hear the go tone, press {action} as fast as you can. Press too early and you lose the round. Your reaction time is your score: faster is better. Best of several rounds.
game.quickdraw.name = Quick Draw
game.quickdraw.unit = points
game.racer.desc = Drive a track you can only hear.
game.racer.help = Hold {left} and {right} to steer. The engine hums where your car is. Gravel roars in the ear you are drifting towards. Cones beep from the lane they block: swerve around them. Reach the finish line as fast as you can.
game.racer.name = Sound Racer
game.racer.unit = points
game.railroad.desc = Pick the starting track that brings the wagon home.
game.railroad.help = Tracks run side by side away from you, from your left to your right, numbered from one. Between neighbouring tracks sit switches, and a wagon reaching a switch crosses over to the track beside it. Press {action} to hear the route, row by row from where the wagons start to the far end: each switch clicks from its place between its two tracks. Then the station bell rings from the track the wagon must end on. Press the number of the track to start on. Routes grow longer and gain tracks as you go; three wrong tracks and the game is over. In Hardcore the route plays only once.
game.railroad.name = Railroad
game.railroad.unit = points
game.rescue.desc = Fly to the beacons before the air runs out.
game.rescue.help = Survivors call out from somewhere around you. Turn with {left} and {right} and hold up to fly forward. The call gets louder and higher as you close in; press {action} when you are on top of it to pick them up. Each rescue buys you more time.
game.rescue.name = Rescue Mission
game.rescue.unit = survivors
game.reverse.desc = A jumbled scale. Flip the front of it until it rises in order.
game.reverse.help = A line of notes from a scale, jumbled. Put them in order, lowest first, rising to the highest. Your only move is to reverse the front of the line: choose how many notes, from the first, with {left} and {right}, hearing the ones you have chosen, and press {action} to flip them. {up} plays the whole line, {down} reads it as numbers, one for the lowest. Five lines, from five notes to nine; the fewer flips, the more you score.
game.reverse.name = Reverse
game.reverse.unit = points
game.roomsize.desc = How big is the room you are standing in?
game.roomsize.help = A clap echoes around a space. Judge the size from the echo alone: press one for a cupboard, up to five for a cathedral. Press zero to clap again.
game.roomsize.name = Room Size
game.roomsize.unit = correct
game.rpsbeat.desc = Rock, paper, scissors, on the beat, against a rival with habits.
game.rpsbeat.help = Rock, paper, scissors, to a beat: three ticks, then throw on the fourth. {left} is rock, {up} is paper, {right} is scissors. Rock blunts scissors, scissors cut paper, paper wraps rock. You hear the rival's throw: a thud for rock, a rustle for paper, a snip for scissors. A throw off the beat is a foul and counts as a loss. Every rival has a habit, and it changes each match of ten throws: learn it and beat it. Three matches, and the beat quickens.
game.rpsbeat.name = Rock Paper Beat
game.rpsbeat.unit = points
game.running.desc = Keep the total in your head as the numbers come.
game.running.help = A chain of numbers is read out: a starting number, then things to add and take away. Keep the running total in your head, then type it and press {confirm}. The chains grow longer as you go, and every fifth right answer in a row scores a bonus. {action} hears the chain again. A wrong total or running out of time costs one of three lives. In Hardcore the numbers are bigger, the chains longer, and you only hear each chain once.
game.running.name = Running Total
game.running.unit = correct
game.rush.desc = Catch falling coins with your ears.
game.rush.help = Coins drop down three lanes: left, centre and right. Move your basket with {left} and {right} and be in the right lane when a coin lands. Your basket clicks so you always know where it is, and each lane has its own pitch when you move, low on the left. With the Stereo option set to relative to you, a coin heard straight ahead is in your lane; set to fixed to the table, the lanes stay where they are and your basket moves between them. Sixty seconds. Hardcore mode uses five lanes.
game.rush.name = Coin Rush
game.rush.unit = coins
game.sale.desc = So much off. What do you pay?
game.sale.help = A price and a discount are read out: type what you pay after the discount and press {confirm}. Ten percent off a price of eighty is seventy-two. {action} hears it again. The faster, the more it scores; a wrong price or running out of time costs one of three lives. In Hardcore the prices are bigger and the discounts trickier.
game.sale.name = Sale Price
game.sale.unit = correct
game.scalerun.desc = Follow the scale up and down.
game.scalerun.help = A scale climbs and falls. Press up when the next note is higher than the last and down when it is lower. Simple to describe and surprisingly slippery once it speeds up.
game.scalerun.name = Scale Runner
game.scalerun.unit = correct
game.sequence.desc = Four numbers. What comes next?
game.sequence.help = Four numbers of a sequence are read out: type the one that comes next and press {confirm}. The steps may add, take away, double, grow, or add the two before; the patterns get trickier as you go. Backspace corrects, {up} and {down} change the number one at a time, and {action} hears the sequence again. A wrong answer or running out of time costs one of three lives. In Hardcore the trickier patterns come sooner and there is less time.
game.sequence.name = Sequence Finder
game.sequence.unit = correct
game.signalhunt.desc = Tune through the static, lock on, and count the pulses.
game.signalhunt.help = A radio telescope listening for signals. Hold {left} and {right} to turn the dial through the static: somewhere on it a signal pulses, faint at first and clearer as you tune closer, with a bright ping when you are locked right on it. Each signal pulses a number of times, from one to nine, then pauses and repeats. Type that number to decode it. The sooner you decode, the more it scores; a wrong number costs points, and each signal fades after twenty-five seconds. Eight signals in all. In Hardcore the signals are fainter and narrower.
game.signalhunt.name = Signal Hunt
game.signalhunt.unit = points
game.skeeball.desc = Nine balls, five rings, and two pockets worth a hundred.
game.skeeball.help = Roll nine balls up the lane into the scoring rings. The rings lie further and further up the lane, worth ten, twenty, thirty, forty and fifty, and before each ball they chime in turn, higher for the further ones. In the two top corners sit small pockets worth a hundred. Aim with {left} and {right}: your aim ticks from where you point. Hold {action}: a power tone rises, and letting go rolls the ball. Too gentle and it falls short for nothing; too hard and it bounces back into the ten ring. To reach a corner pocket, aim right out to the side and roll hard. In Hardcore the power rises faster and the corner pockets are narrower.
game.skeeball.name = Skee-Ball
game.skeeball.unit = points
game.skeet.desc = Pull! Track the clay across the sky and fire.
game.skeet.help = Twenty-five clays. Each one is launched with a call of pull, from the high house on the left or the low house on the right, and whistles across in front of you; the higher its whistle, the higher it flies, and it falls in pitch as it drops. Swing your gun with {left} and {right}: a click comes from where you aim, and a bright ping when you are on the clay. Press {action} to fire. One shot a clay, and from the sixteenth on, pairs: two clays at once, two shots. A hit scores twenty-five, more the earlier you break it. Hardcore has faster clays and a tighter shot.
game.skeet.name = Skeet Shooting
game.skeet.unit = points
game.slalom.desc = Ski the gates by ear, tuck for speed.
game.slalom.help = Thirty gates down the mountain. Each gate flaps from where it stands, left or right of you, louder as it comes up. Steer with {left} and {right}; a soft swish tells you where your skis are. Pass through each gate: a bright tone when you make it, a dull one when you miss it, which adds three seconds. Hold {up} to tuck for speed, but you steer more slowly in a tuck. The faster your time, the more you score.
game.slalom.name = Slalom
game.slalom.unit = points
game.slide.desc = Slide numbered tiles back into order around the one gap.
game.slide.help = Numbered tiles in a frame with one gap, three by three at first and four by four from the fourth puzzle. The arrows slide a tile into the gap: {right} moves the tile on the left of the gap to the right, and so on. Each tile says its number and plays its own note as it slides, one the lowest. Put them in order, one in the top left, reading along each row, with the gap last. Press {action} to hear the row the gap is on, {confirm} to hear the whole frame, and {status} for where the gap is. Fewer slides earn more points.
game.slide.name = Tile Slide
game.slide.unit = points
game.slingshot.desc = Fall past the planet and fire your engine at the closest point.
game.slingshot.help = Your probe swings past a giant planet to steal some of its speed. As you fall toward it, your speed hums higher and faster, and the planet's rumble grows; at the closest point, the hum peaks, and then it starts to fall. Fire your engine with {action} right at the peak for the biggest boost: the nearer the moment, the more speed you gain. Once is all you get on each pass. Ten passes, each at a different speed.
game.slingshot.name = Slingshot
game.slingshot.unit = points
game.snake.desc = Eat, grow, and hear your own coil close in. After Oriol Gomez's COIL.
game.snake.help = You steer a snake around a walled board with {dirs}: up is always north, straight ahead of you, and nothing ever turns. The snake waits until you choose a way to go, then moves by itself, a little faster with every bite. Every arrow turns you that way at once; the way you came turns the snake round, to go tail first. Whatever blocks you, up to five squares away, ticks from its side: north ahead and higher, east on your right, west on your left; the closer it is, the faster and louder it ticks. Your own body ticks brighter than a wall. The food calls from where it is, dead centre only when it is in your own column, with a bright ping on top. Eat it to grow; run into a wall or yourself and you lose one of three lives. Each bite is worth more the more you have eaten. The round lasts five minutes; Hardcore starts faster. After COIL by Oriol Gomez.
game.snake.name = Snake
game.snake.unit = points
game.sneak.desc = Move only when the room is loud.
game.sneak.help = A guard patrols ahead of you. Machinery in the room rises and falls: while it is loud, hold up to creep forward and your footsteps are covered. When it goes quiet, stop dead. The guard's footsteps tell you how close he is.
game.sneak.name = Sneak
game.sneak.unit = guards
game.sniper.desc = Aim by ear alone.
game.sniper.help = Targets chirp somewhere in the stereo field. Sweep your scope with {left} and {right}: it whistles higher the closer you are to the target. Fire with {action}. Forty five seconds.
game.sniper.name = Echo Sniper
game.sniper.unit = points
game.sokoban.desc = Push every crate onto a pad.
game.sokoban.help = Sokoban for the ear. Arrow keys move and push. North is always in front of you, east to your right. Space scans all four directions. Tab reads the nearest crate and pad. U undoes; R, or {confirm} twice, restarts the level. Crates can be pushed, never pulled, so think first. A crate on a pad stays put unless you push it twice in a row.
game.sokoban.name = Warehouse Shift
game.sokoban.unit = points
game.sorting.desc = Every parcel has a bin. Learn the chimes.
game.sorting.help = Parcels arrive one at a time, each chiming the bin it belongs in. Press one, two or three for the low, middle or high bin. Press zero to hear the parcel again. The belt speeds up as the night goes on.
game.sorting.name = Sorting Office
game.sorting.unit = parcels
game.soundorder.desc = Learn the numbers, then name them.
game.soundorder.help = First you hear a set of sounds, each announced with its number. Learn them. Then they play again in a jumbled order with no numbers, and for each one you press the number it belongs to. The set grows every round.
game.soundorder.name = Sound Order
game.soundorder.unit = correct
game.splat.desc = Free fall on eight worlds. Open the chute as late as you dare.
game.splat.help = Eight parachute jumps, each on a different world: the Moon, Mars, Earth, Jupiter and more, each with its own pull, so you fall at a different rate and reach a different top speed. An altimeter beeps faster and higher the nearer the ground, and the height is called every thousand feet. Press {action} to open your parachute. It takes a second and a half to open, so allow for it: the lower it is fully open, the more you score, but if the ground comes first, splat. Press {up} to hear your height and speed.
game.splat.name = Splat
game.splat.unit = points
game.spotsound.desc = Catch the one sound you were given among its lookalikes.
game.spotsound.help = Each round begins with the target sound, played twice, once in Hardcore. Then a stream of sounds follows: most are decoys, close to the target in pitch or in colour, and somewhere among them the target itself plays once. Press {action} the moment you hear it: the faster, the more it scores. Pressing on a decoy, or letting the target slip past, costs one of your three chances. The stream quickens and the decoys creep closer as you go. Press zero to hear the target again before the stream starts.
game.spotsound.name = Spot The Sound
game.spotsound.unit = points
game.sprint.desc = Explode off the blocks and out-run three rivals.
game.sprint.help = Three races of a hundred metres against three rivals, whose footsteps you hear in the lanes beside you. On your marks, set, then the gun: press {left} and {right} one after the other to run, and the faster you alternate, the faster you go. The same key twice stumbles. Pressing before the gun is a false start, and two in one race disqualify you. A whistle marks fifty metres and a rising tone the last ten. Your time is called at the line; faster times score more, and winning a race scores a bonus.
game.sprint.name = 100 Metres
game.sprint.unit = points
game.statues.desc = Keep walking, but freeze before the flash.
game.statues.help = Hold {up} to walk forward to the end of the field. A steady beat plays: beats one, two and three tick, and beat four is a flash. The third tick is higher, as a warning. When the flash comes you must already be standing perfectly still, or you are caught and lose a life. Cross the field and the next one comes at a faster beat. Three lives; in Hardcore you must be still for longer before each flash.
game.statues.name = Statues
game.statues.unit = points
game.sticks.desc = Take sticks. Do not take the last one.
game.sticks.help = A pile of sticks sits between you and your opponent. You take turns, and on your turn you may take one, two or three sticks by pressing one, two or three. Whoever is forced to take the very last stick loses. Every stick taken makes its own sound: yours on your left, your opponent's on your right. Press {action} or {confirm} to hear how many are left. There is a way to win every time, if you can find it.
game.sticks.name = The Stick Game
game.sticks.unit = wins
game.stilts.desc = Left, right, left, right. Do not rush.
game.stilts.help = Walking on stilts means alternating feet in time. Press {left} and {right} alternately, in rhythm with the drum. Press the same foot twice or fall out of time and over you go.
game.stilts.name = Stilt Walk
game.stilts.unit = paces
game.streetball.desc = One on one to twenty-one: drive, shoot, and defend.
game.streetball.help = One on one, first to twenty-one, taking turns with the ball. With the ball, your defender shuffles in front of you, from where he is. Drive past him with {left} or {right}, away from him, for an easy layup worth two; or press {up} to pull up and shoot: aim at the hoop's call with {left} and {right}, then hold {action} and let go at the right power, as in Free Throws. A shot from outside is worth three. On defence, their player dribbles one way: step with {left} or {right} to the side you hear him go, and press {up} to block the moment he grunts to shoot.
game.streetball.name = Street Ball
game.streetball.unit = points
game.sudoku.desc = Fill the grid so every row, column and box holds each number once.
game.sudoku.help = A small sudoku: four by four at first, six by six from the fourth grid. Every row, every column and every box must hold each number exactly once, and each number has its own note, one the lowest. Move with {dirs}: a filled square plays its note and says its number, an empty one gives a soft tick. Type a number to fill the square you are on; a wrong number costs a life. Press {action} to hear the whole row as notes, with a tick for each gap, and {confirm} to hear the whole column. Press {status} for your place. Solve grids for points before the time runs out.
game.sudoku.name = Tone Sudoku
game.sudoku.unit = points
game.sundial.desc = Where is the sun? Then what time is it?
game.sundial.help = The sun crosses the sky from your right to your left: it rises on your right at six in the morning, is highest and highest pitched at noon straight ahead, and sets on your left at six in the evening. Each round the sun sounds from where it is. Set your guess of the time with {up} and {down}, an hour at a time, half an hour in Hardcore, and press {confirm}. Exact scores best, an hour out still scores; further out costs one of three chances. Press zero to hear the sun again, not in Hardcore.
game.sundial.name = Sundial
game.sundial.unit = points
game.swamp.desc = Only some of this ground holds your weight.
game.swamp.help = You cross the swamp one step at a time. At every step there are two places to put your foot, one on your left and one on your right, and only one of them is solid. As you arrive, both sides sound on their own: solid ground gives a firm low thud, quicksand a wet hiss. Press {left} or {right} to step onto that side. Press {action} to hear both sides again. Step into quicksand and you go back to the start, so remember the route.
game.swamp.name = The Swamp
game.swamp.unit = crossings
game.swim.desc = Two lengths against a rival, stroke by stroke.
game.swim.help = A hundred-metre race, two lengths of the pool, against a rival in the lane on your right. Swim with {left} and {right} in turn, one arm then the other: the steadier and quicker your strokes, the faster you go, and the same arm twice splashes and slows you. Every few strokes a rising tone asks for a breath: press {up} for it, or you tire. Near the wall a knock grows louder: press {action} for a tumble turn when it is close. The rival splashes to your right, louder when ahead of you. Hardcore has a faster rival.
game.swim.name = Swimming
game.swim.unit = points
game.switchboard.desc = Connect the caller to the line that answers.
game.switchboard.help = A caller hums on your board. Somewhere along the row a socket hums the same note, heard from its direction. Move with {left} and {right} to find it and press {action} to connect. A wrong plug fumbles the cable for a moment, and three wrong plugs on the same call make the caller hang up. Callers grow impatient, and an impatient caller buzzes faster; they grow less patient the busier the shift gets, and every five calls the board gains a socket. Three dropped calls and the shift is over.
game.switchboard.name = Switchboard
game.switchboard.unit = calls
game.syncopate.desc = Play between the beats, not on them.
game.syncopate.help = A steady pulse plays. Your job is to press {action} exactly between two beats, in the gaps, never on the beat itself. It is much harder than playing along, and it is the foundation of every groove there is.
game.syncopate.name = Off Beat
game.syncopate.unit = offbeats
game.tables.desc = Quick multiplication, read out loud.
game.tables.help = A multiplication is read out: type the answer with the number keys and press {confirm}. Backspace corrects, {up} and {down} change the number one at a time, and {action} hears the question again. Answer before the ticking runs out; the faster you are, the more it scores, and every fifth right answer in a row scores a bonus. A wrong answer or running out of time costs one of three lives. The tables grow as you go. In Hardcore the tables go up to fifteen, some questions are divisions, and there is less time.
game.tables.name = Times Tables
game.tables.unit = correct
game.tanks.desc = Turn the turret to the rumble, fire, and dodge the shells.
game.tanks.help = Three waves of enemy tanks roll around you, each one a low engine rumble from where it is. Turn your turret with {left} and {right}: a click comes from where you aim, and a bright ping when you are on a tank. Press {action} to fire; the shell takes a moment to land, so lead a moving tank a little. When a tank fires at you, you hear its boom and the shell whistling down: press {up} or {down} to roll out of the way before it lands. Three hits and you are out. Each wave has more tanks, and quicker ones.
game.tanks.name = Tank Battle
game.tanks.unit = points
game.target.desc = Make the target from the numbers you are given.
game.target.help = You are given a target and a few numbers. Make the target by typing a calculation with the number keys and plus, minus, star for times and slash for divide, then press {confirm}. It is worked out from left to right like a pocket calculator, so six plus four times three is thirty. Each number may be used once at most, and you need not use them all. Backspace corrects; {action} hears the puzzle and your calculation so far. Every puzzle can be solved. A wrong total or running out of time costs one of three lives. In Hardcore there are more numbers, bigger targets and less time.
game.target.name = Target Number
game.target.unit = correct
game.taxi.desc = Avenues A to H, streets one to eight. Get them there on time.
game.taxi.help = You drive a taxi in a grid city. The avenues run north and south, lettered A to H from west to east; the streets run east and west, numbered one to eight from south to north. Each passenger names a corner, such as D Avenue and 5th Street: drive there one block at a time with {dirs}, east for later letters and north for higher numbers. Each corner is said as you reach it, and {status} tells you where you are and how long your shift has left. Your shift is three minutes, and dropping a passenger never adds to it: the more you deliver, and the longer their rides, the more you score. Roadworks close some blocks, and you will hit the barrier; traffic jams slow you down. {action} repeats where the passenger is going. In Hardcore corners are not said as you drive and the shift is shorter, with more roadworks.
game.taxi.name = Taxi Driver
game.taxi.unit = points
game.telegraph.desc = Short, long, short. Send it back.
game.telegraph.help = A message arrives as short and long taps. Send it back with {action}: a quick press is a short, a held press is a long. The messages get longer. Rhythm is all that matters, not speed.
game.telegraph.name = Telegraph
game.telegraph.unit = messages
game.tempo.desc = Keep the beat after the music stops.
game.tempo.help = A metronome gives you four beats, then falls silent. Keep tapping space on the beat. Every accurate tap scores. Drift too far and the round ends. Each round the tempo changes.
game.tempo.name = Tempo Lock
game.tempo.unit = beats
game.tennis.desc = A real court, a real ball, real scoring. After Oriol Gomez's Tennis.
game.tennis.help = You stand at the south end of a singles court; the net is in front of you and the opponent beyond it. Walk around your half with {dirs}. The ball whooshes from where it is, louder as it comes to you, and knocks where it bounces. Once it has bounced on your side and is within about two metres, swing: D for a forehand, when it is on your right; A for a backhand, on your left; S to smash a high ball. To serve, press D, A or S: the ball must land in the box diagonally across the net. Points are scored as in tennis, love, fifteen, thirty, forty, deuce and advantage, and called out after each one; the first to three games wins the match, and if the round's five minutes run out, whoever is ahead. After Tennis by Oriol Gomez.
game.tennis.name = Tennis
game.tennis.unit = points
game.throw.desc = As far as you can, and not one step further.
game.throw.help = Before each throw you hear how far away the edge is: a low tone for a short track, a high one for a long track, and the distance is read out. Hold {action} and a power tone rises; let go to throw. The further you land, the more it scores, but land beyond the edge and the throw is lost. Ten throws. In Hardcore the power rises faster and the distance is not read out: judge it from the tone.
game.throw.name = The Throw
game.throw.unit = points
game.tightrope.desc = Keep your balance, one small correction at a time.
game.tightrope.help = You are on a wire. You tip slowly to one side and you correct with the opposite arrow. A creak on your left means you are falling left. Small corrections, often. Overcorrect and you will be fighting yourself all the way across.
game.tightrope.name = Tightrope
game.tightrope.unit = steps
game.tincan.desc = The cans rattle. Hit the one that rattles differently.
game.tincan.help = A row of cans rattles in front of you. One of them is weighted and rattles lower than the rest. Move along the row with {left} and {right} and press {action} on the odd one. Guess wrong and the row is reshuffled.
game.tincan.name = Tin Can Alley
game.tincan.unit = cans
game.tk_cyclone.desc = Stop the racing light on the jackpot lamp.
game.tk_cyclone.help = A light races round a ring of twenty-four lamps, ticking from where it is as it goes round you, each lamp a step higher than the last. The jackpot lamp rings a bell as the light passes it. Press {action} to stop the light: on the jackpot you win the whole jackpot, which grows with every play anyone makes on this machine; a lamp either side of it pays ten tickets, and the rest one to three. Three stops a play, each faster than the last.
game.tk_cyclone.name = Cyclone
game.tk_cyclone.unit = tickets
game.tk_pusher.desc = Time your coins to the sweeping shelf and push the pile over the edge.
game.tk_pusher.help = You have ten coins to drop. The pusher shelf sweeps forward and back with a low hum, louder as it comes towards you; a click marks the very front of its sweep. Press {action} to drop a coin: dropped right on the click, it lands just ahead of the shelf and shoves the pile hard; dropped late or early, it only adds to the pile. Coins tumbling over the edge pay tickets, and now and then a golden coin falls with a bright chime, worth fifteen.
game.tk_pusher.name = Coin Pusher
game.tk_pusher.unit = tickets
game.tk_wheel.desc = Hear the segments click by, and brake so the wheel stops on a big one.
game.tk_wheel.help = The wheel spins with a click for every segment that passes under the pointer, and each click is pitched by what that segment pays: the higher, the more tickets, with a bell for the fifty. Press {action} to brake: the wheel always runs on for exactly four more clicks before it stops, so brake four clicks ahead of the segment you want. It slows as it goes, so listen. Three spins a play.
game.tk_wheel.name = Ticket Wheel
game.tk_wheel.unit = tickets
game.tone48.desc = Merge tones into higher octaves.
game.tone48.help = A row of slots holds tones. Press left or right to slide everything that way; equal tones merge into the next octave up. Space reads the row from left to right. Reach the top tone to win. When the row fills with no merges left, it is over.
game.tone48.name = Tone 48
game.tone48.unit = points
game.tower.desc = Move the whole stack, one disc at a time, never big on small.
game.tower.help = Three pegs, left, middle and right, and a stack of discs on the left peg, each disc its own note: the bigger, the lower. Move the whole stack to the right peg. Choose a peg with {left} and {right} and press {action} to lift its top disc; choose another peg and press {action} again to put it down. A disc can never go on a smaller one. {up} reads the pegs. Three towers, of three, four and five discs; the fewer moves you take, the more you score.
game.tower.name = The Tower
game.tower.unit = points
game.traffic.desc = How many went by? Count them as they pass.
game.traffic.help = You stand at the roadside. Cars sweep past both ways, each one an engine note that rises as it comes towards you and falls away as it leaves. Press {up} to count a car and {down} to take one back; each press clicks. When the road goes quiet your count is checked: exact scores best, one out still scores a little, and further out costs one of three chances. In Hardcore, count only the cars going from your left to your right.
game.traffic.name = Traffic Count
game.traffic.unit = points
game.transpose.desc = Play the melody back in a new key, starting from the note you are given.
game.transpose.help = A short melody is played on a scale of eight notes, numbered 1, the lowest, to 8. Then you are told a new starting note: play the same tune with the number keys, beginning there, every step up or down the same as in the original. Press {action} to hear the melody again, and {confirm} to hear your starting note. Each melody you get right adds a note to the next; a wrong note costs one of three lives.
game.transpose.name = Transpose
game.transpose.unit = points
game.trees.desc = The lumberjack needs one exact tree.
game.trees.help = Each round the lumberjack says how tall a tree he needs, from two to ten metres, and you hear that height: a sweep that rises higher and longer for a taller tree. Then you walk through the forest and the trees are heard one by one, each sweep rising to its own height. Press {action} on the tree that matches, while it sounds or just after. Marking a wrong tree, or letting the right one go by, costs one of three chances. In Hardcore the height is not said, only heard, and the trees come faster.
game.trees.name = Tree Scout
game.trees.unit = points
game.truefalse.desc = Is the sum right? Quick!
game.truefalse.help = A sum and an answer are read out. Press {right} if it is true and {left} if it is false, as fast as you can: the quicker, the more it scores. {action} hears it again. A wrong call, or taking too long, costs one of three lives. The sums grow as you go. In Hardcore the wrong answers are closer to the right ones, and there is less time.
game.truefalse.name = True or False
game.truefalse.unit = correct
game.tube.desc = Ride the rim, fire down the tube.
game.tube.help = You ride the rim of a sixteen lane tube. Left and right move you around it, space fires inward. Enemies climb toward you: a threat in your own lane sounds dead centre, others pan to the side you should move toward. Tankers take two hits.
game.tube.name = Tempest Tube
game.tube.unit = points
game.tuner.desc = Find the station in the static.
game.tuner.help = Static hisses across the dial. Somewhere in it a station is playing. Move the dial with {left} and {right}: the closer you are, the clearer it gets and the quieter the hiss. Press {action} when you think you are on it.
game.tuner.name = Radio Tuner
game.tuner.unit = stations
game.tuning.desc = Bring the note into tune.
game.tuning.help = A reference note holds steady while a second sits beside it, slightly out. Move the second with {up} and {down} until the wobble between them disappears, then press {action}. The wobble itself is the instrument: it slows to nothing as you close in.
game.tuning.name = Tuning Fork
game.tuning.unit = notes
game.valves.desc = Spin the wheels shut before the pipes burst.
game.valves.help = Valves stand in a row in front of you, on keys one to four, five in Hardcore. When a pipe starts leaking you hear it hiss from its place, louder and higher as the pressure builds. Press a valve's number to step to it, then turn its wheel shut by pressing the arrows round clockwise: up, right, down, left, and on round again. Each step clicks; three full turns close the valve. Let a pipe's pressure build all the way and it bursts, costing a life. Three lives. In Hardcore one wheel is fitted the other way round and turns anticlockwise.
game.valves.name = Valve Room
game.valves.unit = points
game.vault.desc = Peg solitaire, played by ear.
game.vault.help = Jump a peg over an adjacent peg into the empty hole beyond, and the jumped peg is removed. Arrow keys move your cursor, space picks up and jumps, tab reads the row. Reduce the board to one peg. Every board is generated solvable.
game.vault.name = Vault
game.vault.unit = pegs cleared
game.videopoker.desc = Jacks or better: hold the cards you want and draw the rest.
game.videopoker.help = Video poker, jacks or better. You start with a hundred credits and bet five a hand. Five cards are dealt and read out. Press the keys one to five to hold or release each card, or move along them with {left} and {right} and press {action}. Press {confirm} to draw new cards for every card you are not holding. A pair of jacks or better pays your bet back, two pair twice, and so on up to a royal flush, which pays two hundred and fifty times. {up} reads the hand again with what you hold, {down} the pay table. Twenty-five hands, or until the credits run out; what you finish with is your score.
game.videopoker.name = Video Poker
game.videopoker.unit = points
game.waiter.desc = Take the order, fetch it, bring it back.
game.waiter.help = You are waiting tables. A customer calls from a table: go to them with {left} and {right} and press {action} to hear their order. Then walk to the counter at the far right and press {action} to collect it, and carry it back to the same table. Forget which table and you will be walking a while. Press tab to recall your current order.
game.waiter.name = Table Service
game.waiter.unit = orders
game.weight.desc = How heavy was that thud?
game.weight.help = An object drops. Judge its weight from one to five and press that number. A light thing bounces several times before it settles and sounds high; a heavy thing lands with a single low thud. Weight one bounces five times, weight five lands once. Press zero to hear it again.
game.weight.name = Guess The Weight
game.weight.unit = correct
game.whack.desc = Smack the blips, spare the bombs.
game.whack.help = Posts run from your left to your right, on keys A, S and D. A chirp means whack it fast. A low growl is a bomb: leave it alone. Missing a chirp only costs you the combo, but hitting three bombs ends the game. Hardcore mode widens the row to five posts, on A, S, D, F and G.
game.whack.name = Whack-a-Wave
game.whack.unit = points
game.wheel.desc = Stop the wheel on the prize.
game.wheel.help = A wheel spins, ticking as it passes each segment. One segment rings differently: that is the prize. Press {action} to brake when you think it is under the marker. The wheel spins faster each round.
game.wheel.name = Fortune Wheel
game.wheel.unit = prizes
game.width.desc = How far apart are those two sounds?
game.width.help = Two clicks play, a lower one to the left and a higher one to the right: first one after the other, then together. Judge how far apart they are: press one for almost touching in the middle, up to five for the very edges of your hearing. Press zero to hear them again.
game.width.name = Narrow Or Wide
game.width.unit = correct


# ---- Unlockable items ------------------------------------------

item.engine:acoustic.desc = Physically modelled strings, plucked leads, brushed drums.
item.engine:acoustic.name = Acoustic Engine
item.engine:analog.desc = Warm subtractive synth: detuned saws, sub bass, string pads.
item.engine:analog.name = Analog Engine
item.engine:fm.desc = Bells, electric pianos and brass. The Genesis and DX sound.
item.engine:fm.name = FM Engine
item.engine:hybrid.desc = Analog bed, FM leads, chip percussion. The full mix.
item.engine:hybrid.name = Hybrid Engine
item.game:aceyducey.desc = Two cards up: bet whether the third falls between them.
item.game:aceyducey.name = Acey Ducey
item.game:archery.desc = Draw, hold your aim against the wind, and loose for gold.
item.game:archery.name = Archery
item.game:artillery.desc = Range the target by ear and fire.
item.game:artillery.name = Artillery
item.game:asteroids.desc = Fly, turn and shoot in a field of rocks. After Oriol Gomez's Asteroids.
item.game:asteroids.name = Asteroids
item.game:atc.desc = Land them all. Do not let two meet.
item.game:atc.name = Plane Control
item.game:attack.desc = Did that note begin sharply or gently?
item.game:attack.name = Hard Or Soft
item.game:awari.desc = The ancient sowing game: six pits each, stones, and captures.
item.game:awari.name = Awari
item.game:axe.desc = Spin, spin, and let it fly.
item.game:axe.name = Axe Throw
item.game:backwards.desc = Was that played in reverse?
item.game:backwards.name = Forwards Or Back
item.game:battleship.desc = Find their ships in the dark water before they find yours.
item.game:battleship.name = Battleship
item.game:bearings.desc = Point straight at the sound.
item.game:bearings.name = Bearings
item.game:beatstar.desc = Hear the phrase over the band, then play it back in time.
item.game:beatstar.name = Beatstar
item.game:beeps.desc = A quick burst of beeps. How many?
item.game:beeps.name = Beep Counter
item.game:berzerk.desc = Shoot your way out of the robot maze.
item.game:berzerk.name = Berzerker
item.game:biggersum.desc = Two sums. Which is bigger, left or right?
item.game:biggersum.name = Bigger Sum
item.game:birdsong.desc = Four birds sing, one of them twice: name the one that repeated.
item.game:birdsong.name = Bird Song
item.game:blackjack.desc = Twenty-one, or as close as you dare.
item.game:blackjack.name = Blackjack
item.game:boing.desc = Keep the ball alive, one bounce at a time.
item.game:boing.name = Boing
item.game:bombsaway.desc = Release ahead of the target and let the bomb fall onto it.
item.game:bombsaway.name = Bombs Away
item.game:bounce.desc = Each bounce comes quicker. Hear two, then tap the rest in time.
item.game:bounce.name = Bouncing Ball
item.game:bowling.desc = Ten frames, ten pins, and the pins sing where they stand.
item.game:bowling.name = Bowling
item.game:boxes.desc = Keep your box, or take the offer?
item.game:boxes.name = Mystery Boxes
item.game:boxing.desc = Slip the punch, counter hard, three rounds to win.
item.game:boxing.name = Boxing
item.game:breakout.desc = A wall of bricks, power-ups to catch. After Oriol Gomez's Breakout.
item.game:breakout.name = Breakout
item.game:brightness.desc = Same note, different colour.
item.game:brightness.name = Bright Or Dull
item.game:bugline.desc = Bugs scuttle in from the edges. Swat the nearest.
item.game:bugline.name = Bug Line
item.game:bullfight.desc = The bull charges from one side: step aside at the last moment.
item.game:bullfight.name = The Matador
item.game:bulls.desc = A secret number. How many digits are right, and in the right place?
item.game:bulls.name = Bulls and Cows
item.game:bumblebee.desc = Follow the buzz to the flowers.
item.game:bumblebee.name = Bumblebee
item.game:bumper.desc = Ram them, do not get rammed.
item.game:bumper.name = Bumper Cars
item.game:cctv.desc = Twelve screens, one of them wrong.
item.game:cctv.name = Camera Room
item.game:change.desc = The right change, and quickly.
item.game:change.name = Make Change
item.game:checkers.desc = Draughts on an eight by eight board, captures and kings, against the computer.
item.game:checkers.name = Checkers
item.game:checkpoint.desc = Walk in when the barrier falls silent.
item.game:checkpoint.name = Checkpoint
item.game:chomp.desc = A cookie with a poisoned corner. Do not take the last bite.
item.game:chomp.name = Chomp
item.game:chords.desc = Name what you just heard.
item.game:chords.name = Chord Reader
item.game:chordswitch.desc = Say when the chord changes.
item.game:chordswitch.name = Chord Switch
item.game:claw.desc = Everyone knows it is rigged. Try anyway.
item.game:claw.name = Claw Machine
item.game:climber.desc = Grab each hold on the beat.
item.game:climber.name = Climber
item.game:clock.desc = What time will it be? Clock sums, read out.
item.game:clock.name = Time Keeper
item.game:codebreaker.desc = Find the secret row of tones from bright and soft clues.
item.game:codebreaker.name = Codebreaker
item.game:coins.desc = Coins fall in the jar. How much is there?
item.game:coins.name = Coin Drop
item.game:counterpoint.desc = Follow one line while another distracts you.
item.game:counterpoint.name = Two At Once
item.game:counting.desc = How many was that?
item.game:counting.name = Count The Beeps
item.game:cubehop.desc = Hop the pattern without repeating a square.
item.game:cubehop.name = Cube Hop
item.game:cups.desc = Follow the ball under the shuffling cups.
item.game:cups.name = Cup Tap
item.game:curb.desc = Cross the traffic without looking.
item.game:curb.name = Curb
item.game:curling.desc = Slide the stone to the button, and sweep.
item.game:curling.name = Curling
item.game:darts.desc = Two swings to line up, one throw.
item.game:darts.name = Darts
item.game:decant.desc = Sort the liquids by their pitch.
item.game:decant.name = Decant
item.game:defuse.desc = Cut the wire that does not belong.
item.game:defuse.name = Bomb Defuser
item.game:depthcharge.desc = Sonar pings, a hidden submarine, and a rack of charges.
item.game:depthcharge.name = Depth Charge
item.game:die.desc = Which face is on top after all that rolling?
item.game:die.name = Rolling Die
item.game:digdeep.desc = Something is buried. Listen for the hollow.
item.game:digdeep.name = Dig Deep
