career.all_open = Every hall and wing is open
career.broken = Out of order: {v0} cabinets
career.broken.desc = Play one, any score, and it works again. Each one keeps visitors away.
career.broken.item = {v0}, out of order
career.broken.none = Every cabinet is working.
career.broken.play = Press enter to play it and set it right.
career.broken.title = Out of order
career.ch0 = The lights flicker on in Rhythm Row. Half the drum pads are dead, and the beat machines have forgotten how to count. Mo, the old attendant, hands you a screwdriver: start here, where the music is.
career.ch1 = Neon Alley is dark and dusty, its reflex games sulking in the corner. Mo says the regulars used to queue round the block for these. Get them blinking again.
career.ch2 = The Classic Corner. The machines that built the place, their paddles stiff and their snakes asleep. Mo goes quiet: these were the old owner's favourites.
career.ch3 = The Puzzle Parlour, where nothing moves until you do. Somebody has left a half-finished game on every table. Finish what they started.
career.ch4 = Carnival Row. The coconuts are mouldy and the hoopla stall has lost its hoops. Mo found a crate of fresh prizes in the basement. Time for a show.
career.ch5 = Deep Space is cold. The flight sims have drifted out of tune and the docking clamps grind. Bring them back down to earth, or rather, up to orbit.
career.ch6 = The Night Shift. These cabinets are jobs, and nobody has done them in years. Mo says the night crowd will come back the moment the lights are on.
career.ch7 = The Sound Lab, the quietest hall, where the arcade learns to listen. Tune the instruments; the rest of the building depends on them.
career.ch8 = The Number Hall. The scoreboards are blank and the question machines stammer. Get them counting, and the schools will start booking trips again.
career.ch9 = The Sports Arena, the last hall, and the biggest. The lanes, the pool and the greens are waiting. Finish this, and the arcade is whole again.
career.chapter_of = Chapter {v0} of {v1}
career.ev.charity.desc = Play for a good cause: the town loves you for it, twenty-five reputation at once.
career.ev.charity.name = Charity Marathon
career.ev.family.desc = Balloons and half-price tokens for a day: half as many visitors again.
career.ev.family.name = Family Day
career.ev.intro = {v0} in takings.
career.ev.item = {v0}: {v1} in takings, {v2} days
career.ev.retro.desc = Two nights of the old classics, lights down low.
career.ev.retro.name = Retro Night
career.ev.running = {v0} is on, for {v1} more days. One event at a time.
career.ev.started = {v0} begins! The posters are up all over town.
career.ev.title = Host an event
career.ev.tourney.desc = Three days of competition: every medal you win while it runs is worth five reputation.
career.ev.tourney.name = Tournament Weekend
career.events = Host an event
career.events.desc = A few days that bring the crowds.
career.events.on = Events: {v0} is on
career.finale = The last cabinet hums back to life, and for a moment the whole arcade plays at once. Mo turns the sign on the door to Open. There is a queue outside, all the way round the block. It is yours, and it is the best arcade in town.
career.five_stars = Five stars, the best rating there is. And a gem, from a very happy Mo.
career.fixed = {v0} is working again.
career.grand_finale = The Grand Annex opens to a crowd that fills the street. Mo, in a new waistcoat, rings the bell. People come from three towns away now. The old arcade on the corner is the best in the land, and it is yours.
career.hall_ready = Every job in this hall is done. Visit Arcade Owner to reopen it.
career.intro1 = A letter came this morning. The old arcade on the corner, the one you played in as a child, has been left to you.
career.intro2 = It has seen better days: dark halls, dead cabinets, and no customers but the pigeons. Mo, the attendant, stayed on anyway.
career.intro3b = Repair the cabinets hall by hall, by playing each to its bronze mark. Every repair brings back a little of the arcade's name, and a good name brings visitors, and visitors fill the till every day. Spend the takings on making the place shine, hire staff, put your best cabinets in the window and host events, and the visitors will keep coming.
